1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Margarite Arnesdotter Stovreim==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Arne Stovreim and Queen Of Norway Ingrid Ragnvaldsdatter of Norway - (det som sto her før er slettet siden det gjaldt en helt annen Margareta)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/%C3%86ttesambandet_St%C3%A5rheim_%E2%80%93_Orre_p%C3%A5_J%C3%A6ren_i_mellomalderen Margretha Arnesdotter]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  '''1st gong with Bjørn Bukk ,''' nephew of Erling Skakke , Etne. Bjørn Bukk fell in 1179, the battle of Kalvskinnet near Nidaros . 
2 CONT * Margretha was engaged to the cowling and bellows chief ' '''Simon Kåreson ,''' son of Kåre from Orre on Jæren (Olru-Kåre). According to a Danish source, he was a very rich and noble man. Orre is next door to Reve on Jæren. With 
2 CONC Simon Kåreson,  Margretha Arnesdotter had these children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * a) '''Philip Simonson''' (Philip the Bagler King), d.1217. 
2 CONT *''' b) Andres Simonson ,''' d.1218.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * The Anderson-Krogh genealogy including ancestral lines / compiled by Lester W. Hansen. by Hansen, Lester Welhaven, 1886 - https://archive.org/details/andersonkroghgen00hans/page/74
2 CONT * The family relationship Stårheim - Orre på Jæren in the Middle Ages - https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/%C3%86ttesambandet_St%C3%A5rheim_%E2%80%93_Orre_p%C3%A5_J%C3%A6ren_i_mellomalderen
2 CONT *T he article was originally written by John Thysse at Voll, which states the following sources: Autumn, Sigurd: * 
2 CONT * The history of Norway: with more important sections of the history of Denmark and Sweden. . Published by Gyldendal. Oslo. 1930. Digital version at the Online Library .
2 CONT * Bugge, Alexander: Small contributions to the history of Norway in the 1000s . Christiania. 1914. Digital version at the Online Library .Munch, PA: The Norwegian People's Language and History .
2 CONT * Heimskringla . Sverresoga .
2 CONT * Håkon Håkonsson's soge .
2 CONT * Categories :Genealogy
