1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Baron Gaute Erlingsson Talgje=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Erling Ivarson, til Bjarkoy
2 CONT * Gaute's father was Erling Ivarson av Bjarkoy near Trondenes, south west of Tromso.  He is mentioned in 1263, who married Gregorius Andresson Stovreim daughter Sigrid. Erling's father was Ivar Bjarne son, the son of Bjarne Maards
2 CONC son, mentioned in 1223, and married to Ragna Erlingsdatter, whose father was Erling Vidkunsson, who died about 1182. Gaute made substantial gifts to Alle Helgens church in Bergen, as did his brother Bjarne Erlingsson of Giske. Thi
2 CONC s church was rebuilt in 1266 of stone, after the wooden structure burned down. Gaute Erlingson was also chancellor in Norway twelve years
2 CONT * Gaute Erlingsson was a Norwegian great man. He was one of the kingdom's foremost men during Magnus Lagabøte's reign and in the years after Magnus' death. Gaute was accidentally killed in Stavanger by another chief . He was the f
2 CONC ather of Isak Gautesson.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Sigrid Gregoriusdatter Stovreim''' - Sigrid was married to Baron Gaute Erlingson paa Tolga. He is men- tioned the first time in 1275 as one of King Magnus Haakonson's fore- most men. He became a Baron in 1276 and bef
2 CONC ore that he had been a liegeman. In 1280 he was one of seven chieftains who held the reins of government for the young king Eirik Magnusson. In 1288 he was murdered by a man Halvard av Harde paa Sandeid, who stabbed him, by mistak
2 CONC en identity. This happened in a church yard in Stavanger. Speedy punishment was inflicted upon him by Gaute's son Isak for this terrible deed. In those days it was: an eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth. Baron Isak killed Halvard
2 CONC  as he tried to escape from the church where he was hiding. However, Isak was declared an outlaw arid was compelled to leave the country. He returned again in 1295. Gaute carried a coar of arms described as being a decorated cross
2 CONC  and a closed helmet held up by four arms. - http://www.slektenvonkrogh.no/books/Andersen_Krogh_Genealogy.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT =Their children were:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Isak Gautesson Talgje-Hesby; Birth: circa 1262 inTalgje, Finnøy Municipality, Rogaland, Norway
2 CONT * Eyvor Gautesdatter Talgje; Birth:	circa 1265 in Talgje, Stjernarøy, Finnøy , Rogaland, Norway, married Ogmund Sigurdsson Rova, på Hestbø
2 CONT * Erling Gautesen Talgø; Erling was married to Margareta paa Sudrheim in Sogn. Her parents were Audun paa Slinde, mentioned in 1281, and Gyrid. We can find nothing concerning the life of Erling, but his brother Isak became a Baron
2 CONC  and also an Ambassador. His sister Eyvor was married to Ogmund Sigurdsson of Hestbo, they and the Baron were very prominent people in their locality. Erling and Margareta had a daugh- ter named Holmfrid. Erling died young
2 CONT
2 CONT = STORMANNSTIDA=
2 CONT
2 CONT STORMANNSTIDA The quorum for chieftain power in older times was the same at Tolga as at Hesby, cf. what is said about this garden (b. 1, p. 320). Kyrkja from the middle of the 12th century is a so-called ecclesiastical church, ie.
2 CONC  Built by a great man, and it tells us that it had budd great people at Tolga for a long time before the first representative of Gaute-etched paths in the basements.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Gaute Erlingsson is the first gong member as a member of the king's council in 1277. He is then titled as baron, a title that had been unraveled by the old loincloth (about the lord see bd. I, p. 320). There were only a few p
2 CONC eople who achieved such high rank; In the king's council in 1277, which spoke the foremost men in the country, met seven Baronesses beside Gaute in Tolga.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later we meet Gaute in several contexts, i.a. as syslemann in Stavanger, until 1288 when he was killed. It is an Icelandic story that tells about the murder, which must have happened by cit accident.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to a daughter of the high-standing Gregorius Andersson and was thus linked directly to the royal family: Gregorius was married to Cecilie Håkonsdtr., Daughter of King Håkon Håkonsson born outside of marriage. As we 
2 CONC saw under the mention of Hesby (bd. 1, p. 321), there is much to suggest that the somewhat younger gentleman in this garden, Ogmund Sigurdsson, also had royal blood in the years.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family connections to the royal house place familiane in Tolga and Hesby in the foremost line between the Norwegian great men. There were also new family ties: Eyvor, daughter of Gaute Erlingsson, married to Mr Ogmund at Hesby
2 CONC , so here it was royal blood on both sides. Gaute also had his sons Isaac, who took over Tolga after his father, and Håkon, who was married to the heiress Holmfrid Erlingsdtr .; They bid on Reve in Klepp and had drilled Gaute (no.
2 CONC  4 below) and Margareta, married to Torstein Mita from Bergen.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2. Isak Gautesson was born born approx. 1243 and arrived early in active royalty. 1 128 1 while he was still knight, he was a member of a delegation who was sent to Scotland to negotiate marriage between King Erik Håkonsson and 
2 CONC the daughter of the Scottish king. Such marriage targets were important government documents at that time. King Erik was not yet of age, and some of the members of the Norwegian delegation, between Isaac, were held that in Scotlan
2 CONC d hostage to the king, marital age and conditions that the shooting king asked reached were met. As far as above, Isaac took hold of the murder of his father and dropped his killer. It happened in Stavanger Cathedral, and the murd
2 CONC er resulted in him being willingly laid out. 11295 where he was merciful to and re-entered as a counselor for King Erik and later for his brother Håkon 5. Then he had the title of Baron. It was tragic while he was willing to expla
2 CONC in that he found his wife, a daughter of the Danish Count Jakob Nielssøn of North Halland. The Count was in conflict with the Danish royal family and applied for support in Norway. Isak is not a member of any source after 1302. We
2 CONC  know that he had several ships and trade with England. Isak Gautesson had the son Gaute (no. 3 below) and daughter Cecilie, who was married to the knight Martin Torulvsson at Idse. There is much that suggests that he also had a t
2 CONC hird child, a daughter who in the literature has been called "Feather Princess" (see below 3 below).
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3. Gaute Isaksson did not reach the baroque group such as his father and grandfather, but it may be that he belonged to a younger generation; Baronite speech was abolished by Håkon 5. in 1308. Gaute was a knight, and he was one 
2 CONC of those who in 1319 wrote under the so-called Oslo treaty that guaranteed the royal community between Norway and Sweden, an act which initiated union time in the middle age. Gaute was married to IngebjØrg Jonsdtr. from the square
2 CONC  Kvåle in Sogn. Ho was of high burden and was mentioned in the cellars with a wife's title. Gaute was a sibling in Ryfylke and is mentioned in the basement from 1313 and 1320. This past year he conducted a gift letter with Mrs. In
2 CONC gebjØrg, and they must then have gotten up in Aust-Agder. This may indicate that at that time Gaute had returned from the position of sailor in Stavanger. Whatever the reason may be for him to stay on Agder, we do not know. One of
2 CONC  those who was present when the gift certificate was issued, was Sira Torgils from Fjære, and here it is natural to plug in "Feather Princess". 11320 it must have been clear that Mr Gaute and Mrs. IngebjØrg could not get a boom, j
2 CONC ust as the background for what the letter they are carrying out this year. The letter has divergent more parties that have been destroyed, but we think we can get it. Gaute and IngebjØrg know that virgin Sigrid had trulova with Re
2 CONC idar Dagfinnsson, and they pick up the coveted he gave. As a condition where the goods should fall back if they did not get children together (there was no boom in the marriage, so the goods fall back). The letter has to be thrown
2 CONC  out so that Virgin Sigrid was one
2 CONT
