1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Eyvor Gautesdatter Talgje=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Baron Gaute Paa Erlingsson Talgje and Sigrid Gregoriusdatter Stovreim 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 1265 in Talgje, Stjernarøy, Finnøy , Rogaland, Norway
2 CONT * Death:	after 1328 in Hesby, Finnøy, Rogaland, Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marriage: '''Eyvor Gautesdotter,''' N. 1328, was married to '''Ogmund Sigurdson of Hesby, Finnøy.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Finn Ogmundsson Ridder, til Hestbø,'''  D. 1343, married to Mrs. Gudrun Sæbjørnsdotter. Randa. Dotter to Sæbjørn Helgeson, from Hordaland, Riddar in 1299, 1302 Baron and Reichråd, married to Ragnhild (Ragna) Jonsdotter. 
2 CONT * '''Ivar Ogmundsson Rova;'''  D. 1350, Drottsete. Ivar Ogmundsen HESBØ / ROVA 1362178, Ivar Ogmundsen HESBØ / ROVA was born on / in Hesbø, Finnøy, Rogaland circa 1290. He died in 1350 at / in Rova, Sauherad, Telemark. He was the 
2 CONC son of Ogmund Sigurdsen HESBØ / ROVA and Eyvor Gautesdatter TALGJE.  He was Governor of Skien. He was the Riksråd in 1320. He was a chieftain at Båhus from 1321 to 29.
2 CONT *''' Torstein Ogmundsson Hesbo; Født: Hesbø, Finnøy, Rogaland
2 CONT
2 CONT =Nr: 611 Date: 1328 Aug 14 Location: Bergen=
2 CONT
2 CONT Regest: Appraisal letter from Finn Ogmundsson, Governor of Bergen, Svein Sigurdsson, fehirde in Bergen, Henrik, cannabis at the Apostel Church, Tord, priest at Mariakirken, Einar Torgilsson, Magne at Æyrum, Torgeir [Bjørnsson] 1 a
2 CONC t Stedje, Ivar in Henriksgården and Bjornsson 1 at Stedje, Ivar in Henriksgården and Svein in the pig: After praying from Holmfrid Erlingsdatter and her daughter Mrs Margreta in Roddo huss they went over to the beach to appreciate
2 CONC  the goods Margreta had at home in Torstein mita's farm, and which [now?] was moved east in Viken. On behalf of Torstein, Sira Einar was present. The goods are listed in detail; There were in total textiles (house bunad and clothe
2 CONC s) for 172 mark bounty, a psalter worth 3 mark, gold and silver (in English money, tubs and jewelry) for 146 mark - in all goods worth 321 mark bounty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Present were Mrs Ragnhild Jonsdatter, Mrs. Øyvora Gautesdatter, Mrs Rønnaug Reppisdatter, Mrs Sunniva Brynjulvsdatter, Mrs Gyrid Sigurdsdatter, Herdis Torvaldsdatter and Margreta Petersdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sealed by the issuers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Orig (perg): AM 22.11 - Kbh. Printed: DN II no. 165. 1 backJfr NSig I no 73.
2 CONT
