1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *  5. juli 1445
2 CONT
2 CONT Biskop Thorlars i Viborg, Erik Nielsen Gyldenstjerne til Tim, høvedsmand på Aalborghus, Niels Eriksen, Erik Eriksen, Peder Eriksen og Jens Madsen udsteder vidne, at '''Jep Axelsen (Thott)''' lovede at lade Aalborg Helligaandshus u
2 CONC hindret nyde Kalstrup og Kalstrup mølle.
2 CONT
2 CONT RA, NKR nr. 3534. Tidligere Aalborg Hellgåndskloster. Perg. [6] segl. Efter Danske Magazin:1 seglfragm. og 5 pergamentremme. Efter Rep. II, 7523: 1. Utydeligt. 2. [Gxvi17 Gyldenstjerne] 5. [Gxvi20]. Efter L. Dipl er 2, 3 og 5 Gyld
2 CONC enstjernes våben. Omtalt i Helligåndsklostre nr. 46. Jexlev, Gejst. ark. II, s. 133. Rep. II nr. 7523. Danske Mag. 5,2, s. 185.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alla men, thette breff see heller høra læses, helsa wy Thorlaff, met guds nadhe biscop i Wyborgh, Erik Nielsson aff Tiim, riddaræ och høwitzman pa Alborghus, Nielss Ericson, Eric Ericsson, Pædher Erikson och Jess Mattisson, riddær
2 CONC a, kerlig met gud oc kungøre, at aar epter gudz børdh mcdxl pa thet fempta then mandagh nest epter war frwæ dagh visitacionis wara wy och manghæ andhræ gothe mæn skikkade i grabrødhre closter j Alborg, hørde och saghæ, at walboren
2 CONC  man Jæpp Axelsson fullelighe tilstodh och aldhelis staducht och fast holde vilde, thet helghandzhuset j forne Alborg matte whinderlige nydhe och hawa Kalstrop, som ligger j Wygherby sogn j Hymersyssell, met mølle stedh j thet sam
2 CONC a steth met thera tillegilssæ j alla madhe, som fordis J'''æppe Axelsons keræ moder, frw Elsø aff Stoffringhe,''' thet til forne gifuit hafde. Jn quorum omnium et singulorum fidem et testimonij euidenciam sigilla nostra presentibu
2 CONC s sunt appensa. Datum et actum anno, die et loco supradictis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://protokoller.dk/diplomatariumhornumnse/Diplomatarium%20Hornumense%20del%201.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT * 
2 CONT
2 CONT After Palne Jensen was Niels Bugge probably the owner of Støvringgård. Hr. Palne's and fru Eline's daughter was his first wife. It is known that Eline Buggesdatter and her husband hr. Christiern Vendelbo, who died ab.1400, owned t
2 CONC he farm, and after Christiern Vendelbo's death it came via inheritance to the daughter Else. "Fru Elseff af Steuringe" was the first time married to Axel Jepsen, who belonged to the Jutland lineage of the Thotts, and the second ti
2 CONC me to Lyder Holck, who in 1434 and 1437 is mentioned of Steuringe. After fru Else's death came Støvringe to her son of first marriage Jep Axelsen Thott and then to his son Axel Jepsen, who died in the last fourth of the 15th centu
2 CONC ry. Other relatives had possibly also owner-ship of the farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thyrashm.blogspot.dk/2010/05/stvringgard-east-jutland-randers-amt.html
