1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cecilia kan ikke ha vært datter av sysselmann Ivar Ogmundsson Rova og stammor for slekta på Lindheim samtidig, fordi Ivar ikke hadde etterkommere da han døde. Hvis han hadde hatt etterkommere ville ikke arven hans 
2 CONC ha gått til brorsønnen Ogmund Finnson, men til livsarvingene, som Cecilia og hennes barn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecilia giftet seg[2808] (1) med Torleiv Saksebjørnsson, født ca 1295 på Lindheim i Sauherad,[2809] død før 1341.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecilia giftet seg[2810] (2) med Vetride Borgarsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT =Cecilia Ivarsdatter Rova=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Ivar Ogmundsson Rova and Kristin Toresdatter Sørum 
2 CONT * born at Nes in Romerike
2 CONT * Cacilie was a relatively rare name in Norway in the Middle Ages, but in some genera you can follow it. Mr Ivar Ogmundsson's great-grandmother was Cecilie.
2 CONT * Mr. Ivar was the Governor of the Skiing Syslaw from 1335. He was sitting on the Dags Family's old family farm Bratsberg, which was probably his own and not good-bye. Mr. Ivar was married to Mrs Kristin Toresdtr. and had two daug
2 CONC hters. Both married in 1341. One was Kristin and married the Swedish armed forces Nils Magnusson to Turku in Sødermannland. The other can not be other than Cecilia on Nes, first married to the hirsman Torleiv Saksabjørnson at Lind
2 CONC heim, and later with Vetrlide Borgarson from Hem in Sauherad. After the information one has, Nes and several farms who have gone out of Nes must have heard of Mr. Ivar and his posterity. If Nes was one of the royal farms of Harald
2 CONC  Grendske, it is good that this farmhouse was excluded for so long.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:circa 1295, at Nes in Romerike
2 CONT * Death:	Nes Søndre, Gjerpen, Telemark, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married (1) - '''Torleiv Saksebjørnsson,''' født ca 1295 på Lindheim i Sauherad,[2838] død før 1341
2 CONT * Married (2) - '''Vetride Borgarsen;'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Torleiv Saksebjørnsson =
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ogmund Torleivsson;'''  He settled in Hybbestad in Tjølling in 1370, but took over Lindheim when his brother Bjørn became governor. He had, as far as we know, four sons
2 CONT * '''Bjørn Torleivsen;''' died after 1397 at Bjørntvet in Solum.  Married Elin Torgeirsdatter Dylla
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Vetride Borgarsen:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Borgar Vetterildeson;''' died 1336 at Hem in Sauherad.  He married Aslaug Saksebjørn's daughter
2 CONT
