2 CONC  the Mediterranean as far as Naples: into Valencia to the south and the Balearic Islands, Sicily and the Kingdom of Naples to the east [the Aragonese Crown had been forced to renounce its claims to territories north of the Pyrenee
2 CONC s, except for James's patrimony of Montpellier, by the Fourth Lateran Council of 1215]. By a treaty with Louis IX of France, he wrested the county of Barcelona from nominal French suzerainty and integrated it into his crown. His p
2 CONC art in the Reconquista was similar in Mediterranean Spain to that of his contemporary Ferdinand III of Castile in Andalusia.
