1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ingerid Sigurdsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Sigurd Syr Halvdansson and Åsta Gudbrandsdóttir, Queen of Norway 
2 CONT * INGERID Sigurdsdatter Snorre names "Guthorm, the eldest, then Gunhild, the next Halfdan, Ingerid and Harald" as the children of Sigurd & his wife. Morkinskinna names (in order) “Gudrødr…Hálfdan…Ingibjorg…Gunnhildr, Haraldr” as t
2 CONC he children of “Sigurdr sýr” and his wife “Ásta daughter of Gudbrandr”[300]. Snorre names "Ingerid, a daughter of Sigurd Syr and Asta" as the mother of Gudrun, daughter of Nefstein
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#NefsteinMIngeridSigudsB Project MedLands Norway Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''NEFSTEIN, son of -- married INGERID Sigurdsdatter,''' daughter of SIGURD Syr King of Ringeringe & his wife Asta Gudbrandsdatter.  Snorre names "Ingerid, a daughter of Sigurd Syr and Asta" as the mother of Gudrun, daughter of Ne
2 CONC fstein[220]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Nefstein & his wife Ingerid Sigurdsdatter had three children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''SIGURD'''  married ---.  The name of Sigurd´s wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sigurd & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>a)         '''SIGURD Sigurdsson''' (-1135).
2 CONT * 2.         '''TORE Ingridsson'''
2 CONT * 3.         '''GUDRUN Nefsteinsdatter''' Snorre records that King Olav gave Skule "his female relative, Gudrun, the daughter of Nefstein…and Ingerid" in marriage[221].  '''married SKULI Tostesson,''' son of [TOSTIG Godwinsson & h
2 CONC is wife Judith de Flandre]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm Project MedLands Norway Kings]
2 CONT
2 CONT SIGURD "Hrise", son of HARALD I "Hårfagre/Harfagri/Fairhair" King of Norway & his fourth wife Snefried .  Snorre names "Sigurd Hrise…Halfdan Haleg, Gudrod Ljome and Ragnvald Rettilbeine" as the four sons of King Harald and his wif
2 CONC e Snæfrid[276].  The Historia Norwegie names "Siwardus…Gigas" as sixth son of "Haraldus Comatus"[277].  Morkinskinna recites the descent of “Harald Sigurdarson” from “Harald hárfagri”, to “Sigurdr hrisi”, to “Hálfdan, father of Si
2 CONC gurdr sýr, the father of Haraldr”, adding that these ancestors were all “kings of Hringaríki in Norway”[278].  Under his father's division of territories, Ringerike, Hadeland, Thoten and their dependencies were granted to his sons
2 CONC  by Snæfrid[279].  m ---.  The name of Sigurd's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sigurd Hrise & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''HALFDAN Sigurdsson'''.  The Historia Norwegie names Halfdan son of "Siwardus Risi…filius Haraldi Comati"[280].  Morkinskinna recites the descent of “Harald Sigurdarson” from “Harald hárfagri”, to “Sigurdr hrisi”, t
2 CONC o “Hálfdan, father of Sigurdr sýr, the father of Haraldr”, adding that these ancestors were all “kings of Hringaríki in Norway”[281].  m ---.  The name of Halfdan's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Halfdan Sigurdsson & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>* a)         '''SIGURD Syr''' (-1018).  The Historia Norwegie names "Siwardus Scroffa rex montanus" as son of Halfdan, son of "Siwardus Risi…filius Haraldi Comati"[282].  Morkinskinna recites the descent of “Harald Sigurdarson”
2 CONC  from “Harald hárfagri”, to “Sigurdr hrisi”, to “Hálfdan, father of Sigurdr sýr, the father of Haraldr”, adding that these ancestors were all “kings of Hringaríki in Norway”[283].  He was christened in 998.  King of Ringeringe.  '
2 CONC ''married (995 or after) as her second husband, ASTA, widow of HARALD "Grenske",''' daughter of GUDBRAND Kula & his wife ---.  The Historia Norwegie records the marriage of "Haroldum Grensca" and "Asta filiam Gudbrandi Culu", and 
2 CONC her second marriage to "Siwardus Scroffa rex montanus" who was the son of Halfdan, son of "Siwardus Risi…filius Haraldi Comati"[284].  Morkinskinna records that “Sigurdr sýr” married “Ásta daughter of Gudbrandr”, previously wife o
2 CONC f “Haraldr grenski”[285].  She and her father are named by Snorre, who also records both her marriages[286].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sigurd Syr & his wife Asta Gudbrandsdotter had five children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>* i)          '''GUTTORM Sigurdsson'''  Snorre names "Guthorm, the eldest, then Gunhild, the next Halfdan, Ingerid and Harald" as the children of Sigurd & his wife[287].  Morkinskinna names (in order) “Gudrødr…Hálfdan…Ingib
2 CONC jorg…Gunnhildr, Haraldr” as the children of “Sigurdr sýr” and his wife “Ásta daughter of Gudbrandr”[288]. 
2 CONT >>>>>>>* ii)         '''GUNHILD'''.  Snorre names "Guthorm, the eldest, then Gunhild, the next Halfdan, Ingerid and Harald" as the children of Sigurd & his wife[289].  Morkinskinna names (in order) “Gudrødr…Hálfdan…Ingibjorg…Gunnh
2 CONC ildr, Haraldr” as the children of “Sigurdr sýr” and his wife “Ásta daughter of Gudbrandr”[290].  Snorre records the marriage of "Ketil Kalf of Ringanes" and "Gunhild, a daughter of Sigurd Syr and King Olaf's mother Asta"[291].  m 
2 CONC ([1025]) KETTIL Kalf of Ringanes, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kettil & his wife GUNHILD Sigurdsdotter  had two children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (a)       '''GUTTHORM'''.  Snorre names Guthorm as son of "Ketil Kalf and Gunhild of Ringanes…a sister's son to King Olaf and Harald Sigurdson", recording that he "had his winter quarters often in Dublin and was in gre
2 CONC at friendship with King Margad"[292].  Morkinskinna records that Tostig, son of Godwin, sent “Gunnhildr´s son Guthormr” to offer Northumbria to Harald III King of Norway in return for help in the conquest of England[293]. 
2 CONT >> >>>>>>>>* (b)       '''SIGRID Kettilsdatter'''' Snorre names "Sigrid, a daughter of Ketil Kalf and Gunhild, King Harald's sister" as the wife of Eindride, son of "Einar Tambaskelfer"[294].  m EINAR Einarsson, son of EINAR Thamb
2 CONC arskelfir & his wife Bergljot Haakonsdatter (-killed in battle [1050]).
2 CONT >>>>>>>>* iii)        '''HALFDAN Sigurdsson''' Snorre names "Guthorm, the eldest, then Gunhild, the next Halfdan, Ingerid and Harald" as the children of Sigurd & his wife[295].  Morkinskinna names (in order) “Gudrødr…Hálfdan…Ingib
2 CONC jorg…Gunnhildr, Haraldr” as the children of “Sigurdr sýr” and his wife “Ásta daughter of Gudbrandr”[296].  m ---.  The name of Halfdan's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Halfdan Sigurdsson & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>>>* (a)       '''THORBERG [Bergliot] Halfdansdatter''' ([1018/20-).  Snorre names "Bergliot, a daughter of Halfdan…son of Sigurd Syr" as the wife of "Fin Arnason"[297].  Her birth date is estimated from the marriage date
2 CONC  of her paternal grandparents, but bearing in mind the tight chronology for the birth of her daughter Ingebjörg.  '''married FIN Arnesson, son of ARNE & his wife''' --- (-1062).  Of Yriar in Austratt Lendermann Norway.  Jarl of Ha
2 CONC lland in Denmark [1051].  Snorre names "Thorberg, Fin and Arne" as the sons of Arne[298]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>* iv)       '''INGERID Sigurdsdatter''' Snorre names "Guthorm, the eldest, then Gunhild, the next Halfdan, Ingerid and Harald" as the children of Sigurd & his wife[299].  Morkinskinna names (in order) “Gudrødr…Hálfdan…Ingi
2 CONC bjorg…Gunnhildr, Haraldr” as the children of “Sigurdr sýr” and his wife “Ásta daughter of Gudbrandr”[300].  Snorre names "Ingerid, a daughter of Sigurd Syr and Asta" as the mother of Gudrun, daughter of Nefstein[301].  married , s
2 CONC on of ---. 
2 CONT >>>>>>>>* v)        '''HARALD Sigurdson''' (1015-killed in battle Stamfordbridge 25 Sep 1066).  Snorre names "Guthorm, the eldest, then Gunhild, the next Halfdan, Ingerid and Harald" as the children of Sigurd & his wife[302].  Mor
2 CONC kinskinna names (in order) “Gudrødr…Hálfdan…Ingibjorg…Gunnhildr, Haraldr” as the children of “Sigurdr sýr” and his wife “Ásta daughter of Gudbrandr”[303].  The Historia Norwegie names Harald as son of "Siwardus Scroffa rex montanu
2 CONC s" & his wife[304].  He succeeded in 1047 as HARALD III "Hardråde" King of Norway. 
2 CONT
