1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Vidkun Jonsson på '''Bjarkøy=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lendmann hos kongene  Magnus Berrføtt og Sigurd Jorsalfare'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *Son of  Jon Arnesson og Ragnhild Sigurdsdatter
2 CONT * 1102 Vidkun was one of the great men who fought with King Magnus Berrføtt in Dublin and Ireland on his voyage on the west road. The king fell in Ireland in 1103.
2 CONT * 1108 Vidkun Jonsson led the crusade of Magnus Berrføtt's son King Sigurd Jorsalfare conducted in Jerusalem from 1108 - 1111 Sigurd Jorsalfar's son Magnus was raised at Vidkun in Bjarkøy.
2 CONT * Pedigree: 27, Vidkun Johnson was one of King Magnus Berrføtt's teammates, He fought with King Magnus in Ireland where the king fell in 1103. Vidkun Johnsen led the crusade King Sigurd Jorsalfar performed in Jerusalem from 1108 -
2 CONC  111.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: a '''daughter of Svend Svendsen of Gjerde'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Erling Vidkunsson, '''(ca 1140 – ca 1182), Erling was born about 1140 on Bjarkøy, died about 1182 on the Romsdal coast. He was married to Ragnild Lodmund's daughter.  Erling was the country's richest and most distinguished ma
2 CONC n. He became a knight in 1316 and was given the title of royal seat in 1323 and the authority to rule the country with royal authority and with the consent of the Council of Ministers under Magnus Eriksson's minor. Erling was rule
2 CONC d for nine years, until 1332, when King Magnus himself took over, and served as chancellor from 1324 to 1327. He was evidently a loyal and restrained man who did not seek to exploit his power to his own advantage. In the 1340s, he
2 CONC  was a governor of Sunnmøre, and still attended important council meetings and exercised his influence in major political matters. He also had large properties.
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Nordic Family Book from 1876 says about Jon Arnesson=
2 CONT
2 CONT lendemann / lendmann These terms were used in medieval times (11th - 13th century) and were titles denoting nobility. The 'lend (er) man' was receiving taxes from the king's landed properties and was often used as an advisor by th
2 CONC e king. He ranked after duke and earl.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) The Bjarkö family. Arne Arnesson was like the brothers Torberg a faithful supporter of Olof den holy, not withstanding he was married to a daughter to Erling Skjalgsson. When Olof returned to Norway, A. joined him and was badly
2 CONC  injured at the Battle of Stiklastad. His son Jon married one daughter of Tore Hund and thereby inherited his tribal goods Bjarkö. Jon's son was the one from Magnus Barefoot's last Ireland train (1103) familiar * Knowledge Jonsson
2 CONC , whose son Erling among them the war belonged to Magnus Erlingsson's party.  Her son Vidkunn Erlingsson remained at the age of 18 (1183) killed by Sverre's followers. With him extended the family, and Bjarkö passed through his si
2 CONC ster Ragnas marriage to the lawyer in Hålogaland Bjarne Mardsson. From them came "the younger Bjarkö family ", who later also inherited Giske.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
