1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.nermo.org/slekt/d0009/g0000074.html#I3924
2 CONT
2 CONT ABT 1475 - ____
2 CONT
2 CONT     * BIRTH: ABT 1475, (?) 'Hustru'
2 CONT
2 CONT     * EVENT: 1493, Samtykket i morens salg av gård i Oslo 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Jóhanna Mattíasdóttir var í föðurætt af ætt, sem komin var út af danska biskupinum Jens Jakobssøn Blik í Osló (1420-53). Hann var einnig Kanslari Elísabetar I af Danmörku. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frú Margreta Johannesdatter hét móðir hennar. Móðurætt hennar var af þýskum ættunum Ziesendorf frá Meklenburg og Gerst frá Pommern, en hvorutveggja þessarra tta tengdust norskum ættum. Ekki verða þær þó raktar lant fram með vissu.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT En í gegnum skydleikann við hertogaættina Suður Jótlandi opnast heldur betur framættarleiðir til merkilegra ætta um gjörvölla Evrópu svo sem konungs- og keisaraætta, hertoga- og markgreifaætta auk fjölmargra greifaætta.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Johanna Mattisdatter was, through her father, Mattis Pedersen, a descendant of the Danish bishop of Oslo, Jens Jakobssøn Blik (1420-53). Jens was also a Chancellor of Elizabeth I of Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Margreta Johannesdatter was her mother's name. Her mother's family was of the German family of Ziesendorf from Mecklenburg and Gerst from Pomerania, but both of these families were related to Norwegian families. However, they 
2 CONC will not be tracked down with certainty.
2 CONT
2 CONT But through the closeness to the ducal family of South Jutland, the lines of descent to notable families all over Europe, such as royal and imperial families, duke and margrave families, as well as numerous count families, open up
2 CONC  even better.
