1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jon Halvardsson Smør'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Født:	cirka 1350 Oslo, Norway (Norge)   
2 CONT * Død:	cirka 1395 (36-53) Bergen, Bergen, Hordaland, Norway (Norge)  
2 CONT * Begravet:	Lavranskirken, Tønsberg, Tønsberg, Vestfold, Norway (Norge)  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nærmeste familie:	
2 CONT * Sønn av Halvard Jonsson Smør og Ingrid Ølversdatter Smør 
2 CONT * Ektemannen til Ingeborg Sigurdsdatter Sudreim; Ragna Ormsteinsdatter og Ukjent Svalesdatter Rømer 
2 CONT * Far til Svale Jonson Smør; Ulvilde Jonsdatter Smør; Sigurd Jonson Smør; Hallvard Jonson Smør; Gaute Jonsson Smør; og Bothilda Jonsdatter Jonsdatter Smør 
2 CONT * Bror av Kristian Halvardsson Smør og Hallkjell Halvardsson Smør 
2 CONT * Halvbror av Ingeborg Hallvardsdatter Smør; Otte Rømer og Harneyt Rømer  
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Alt birth date: 1359
2 CONT
2 CONT Hr Jon Hallvardsson Smør14,24, 17G Grandfather  Birth 1359, Oslo  Death ca 1395, Bergen  Occupation Kongeleg umbudsmann i Bjørgvin 1375. (Bergen)  Alias/AKA Herr Joenn Smør Haluardso  Father Hallvard Jonsson Smør (ca1310-~1395)  M
2 CONC other Ølversdatter (1329-) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses  1 Margrete Svalesdatter Rømer, 17G Grandmother  Birth ca 1360  Death ca 1448  Father Svale Ølversson (~1310-1363) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Svale Jonsson (1389-1442) 
2 CONT  Ulvhild Jonsdatter (1395-) 
2 CONT  Gaute Jonsson (~1395-1442) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Hr Jon Hallvardsson Smør  Lever i 1310. Nevnt i 1375 Bergen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det er ikke mye vi vet om for fedrene til Jon Hallvardson Smør. Men en del spekulativ litteratur som trekker linjene dels tilbake til Erling Skakke og Sigurd Jorsalfar og dels til lendmannen Hallkjell Jonson Huk og Orkenøyjarlene,
2 CONC  har tradisjonelt vært godt lesestoff blant slektsinteresserte med sans for middelalderen. Jeg tar med et av snitt om disse spekulasjonene helt til slutt i dette kapitlet. - Når det gjelder Jon Hallvard sons mor, dvs. Hallvard Jon
2 CONC sons kone, så het hun i følge Leistad NN Ølversdotter. Samtidig synes Leistad å konstatere at vi i dag ikke vet noe om denne Ølver eller hans forferdre. Ellers er det riktig i denne innledningen også å vise til Geirr I. Leistads d
2 CONC røftelse av Smør-navnet der han konkluderer med at navnet var et personlig <tilnavn> og ikke et slektsnavn. Kilde: VFS.  Notes for Margrete Svalesdatter (Spouse 1)  NB! (tvilsom identitet) (NN Svalesdatter) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Notater : Han var i 1375 kongens ombudsmann i Bergen. Mer vites ikke om ham.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Født 1359 i Oslo. Sønn av Hallvar Jonsen Smør og ? Ølversdatter. Han stå som kongens ombudsmann i Bergen omkring 1375. Døde 1395 i Bergen
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 1375 Jgk, ombudsmann i Bergen gift med Rømerætt.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Han var i 1375 kongens ombudsmann i Bergen.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Kongelig umbudsmann i Bjørgvin i 1375.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tre barn: Svale 1389-1442, Ulvhild 1395-, Gaute 1395-1442.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Jon Halvardsson Smør, er nemnd som kongeleg ombodsmann i Bjørgvin i 1375. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT When Jon Halvardsen Smør was born in 1350 in Oslo, Norway, his father, Halvard, was 23 and his mother, Unknown, was 29. He died in 1395 in Bergen, Hordaland, Norway, at the age of 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon Hallvardson Smør (fl. 1375) was a Norwegian nobleman. He was a son of the knight Hallvard Jonson Smør. In 1375, Jon was the ombudsman of king Haakon VI of Norway. He had two known children, the son Svale, and daughter Ulvhild 
2 CONC (whose granddaughter Birgitte married Trond Tordson Benkestok).
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Svale Jonson Smør (c. 1380 – aft. 1442) was a Norwegian knight and riksråd (cabinet minister).Svale was a son of the royal ombudsman Jon Hallvardson Smør. He was one of the most powerful men in Norway in the early 15th cen
2 CONC tury. He lived in Bergen, and in 1404 was the lord of Bergenhus Fortress. In the mid 1420s Svale functioned as a riksråd and participated in settling numerous cases between Norway and Scotland. He is further mentioned as a knight 
2 CONC in 1442, when he was present at the royal coronation of Christopher of Bavaria in Oslo.Svale was married to Sigrid Gunnarsdotter Kane, and in 1412 inherited Hatteberg by Sigrid's uncle Gaute Eirikson of the Galte-family. Together 
2 CONC Svale and Sigrid had the son Jon, and the daughters Bothilda and Inga. In addition, Svale had another daughter, also called Inga (whose great-granddaughter married into the Orm-family) by an otherwise unknown frille (concubine).
2 CONT
2 CONT Smør, or after the coat of arms, "Leopard's head (under chevron)", was the name of a Norwegian medieval family of the high nobility.[1] The family was one of the few original noble families of Norway, as it, unlike many other fami
2 CONC lies, did not originate from Denmark or Sweden. The family owned land in Norway, as well as on the Faroe Islands and Shetland (which at the time was a Norwegian overseas possession). The male line of the family died out in the lat
2 CONC e 15th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT The coat of arms of the Smør-family had a blue background, and a golden Leopard's head under a red chevron.[3] The family is sometimes alternatively called "Leopard's head (under chevron)" after the coat of arms. 
2 CONT ----
