1 OCCU enke, til, levde 1396. Hun var fra gården Herset i Trøgstad sogn Østfold
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Coat of Arms Added  reference 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.myheritage.no/site-family-tree-204982981/hansen?rootIndivudalID=1511126&familyTreeID=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Utdrag fra denne tråden på arkivverkets forum: https://forum.arkivverket.no/topic/128478-43009-var-kristina-gottskalksdatter-torsnes-jondalisland-gift-flere-ganger/?page=2#comment-1055238
2 CONT
2 CONT Sitat Are Gustavsen: "Jeg får supplere med at Rane Eivindsson er nevnt 1349-1362, og hustru Åsa Salmundsdotter 1351-1396. Sistenevnte år skrev hun sitt testamente. Sollied har _gjettet_ på at hustru Åsa kan være en datter av en Sa
2 CONC lmund på Herset i Trøgstad. Rane Eivindssons opphav er ikke påvist."
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://vf.disnorge.no/system/files/DIS-VF/kilder/tonsberg/Helge_Gjessing_-_Tunsbergs_Historie_i_Middelalderen_til_1536_LQ.pdf Helge Gjessing: Tunsbergs historie i middelalderen 1536 - side 96]<br/>
2 CONT [http://www.dokpro.uio.no/perl/middelalder/regest_vise_tekst.prl?b=9430&s=n&str= Regesta Norwegica]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Aase Salmundsdotter''', Selvik
2 CONT
2 CONT Ase was from farm Herset in Trogstad, Ostfold. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Åsa was a widow from Selvik in Sande in Vestfold. She was very rich and in her will of 1396 she gave large donations to churches and monasteries. She chose her burial in Gråbrødre monastery in Tønsberg where her second husband, Ra
2 CONC ne, was buried, and gave the convent 30 mark. She gave a farm to the cathedral in Oslo and Hovedøya Abbey, half to each, so that she and her husband would be remembered by a day on which there would be candles, ringing and alms to
2 CONC  the poor. Two churches received 10 aurabol and a church 2 1/2 aurabol so that there would be an annual mass for her first husband and his parents. Hoff church got 7 aurabol to [memorialize?] herself and her son Eivind. A church g
2 CONC ot 10 aurabol to [memorialize?] her and her father. (An aura was 27 grams of silver.)[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT References ↑ 1.0  1.1  1.2  1.3 Kirkeby, Birger. Buildings book for Sauherad, farms and farms . (Sauherad: Issued by Sauherad municipality, 1980-1988), 4: 517, Ætta from Søum and Reine in Sandsvær. 'Rane Eivindsson, knight, studen
2 CONC t from 1349, fehirde in Tunsberg, gm enka Åsa Salmundsd. to Selvik in Sande in Vestfold (from the house in Trøgstad) d approx. 1396 ' 
2 CONT
2 CONT translation: Rane Eivindsson, knight, mentioned from 1349, treasurer in Tunsberg, married to widow Åsa Salmundsdatter of Selvik in Sande in Vestfold (from Huset in Trøgstad) d ca. 1396.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anderson, Lorna, and Audrey Overland. Overland family history : with roots in Telemark Norway. (River Falls: River Falls Journal Commercial Printing Dept., 1986), 1:94. 'She was from the farm Herst in Trogstad parish Ostfold.'
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 3.0  3.1 Kløvstad, G. O, and Andreas Mørch. Sandeboka: village book for Sande in Vestfold . (Drammen: Published by a Comit ?, 1939), p. 69. ↑ Birth year estimated based on estimated birth years of her husband and daughter, and o
2 CONC n the approx. year she died.
