2 CONC son Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Lothair won the election and banned Frederick, in 1126 Henry abdicated as duke of Bavaria and retired to the family foundation of Weingarten Abbey so that he did not have to take part in the prosecution of his son-in-law. He
2 CONC nry died shortly thereafter and was buried in Weingarten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry and Wulfhild had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith, married Frederick II, Duke of Swabia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad, died 17 March 1126 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry X the Proud 
2 CONT
2 CONT Welf 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia, married Berthold III, Duke of Zähringen and Leopold I, Duke of Styria 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wulfhild, married Rudolf, Count of Bregenz 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathilde, married Diepold IV, Margrave of Vohburg and Gebhard III, Count of Sulzbach 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adalbert, Abbot of Corvey 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Henry IX (died 13 December 1126), called the Black, a member of the House of Welf, was duke of Bavaria from 1120 to 1126.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was the second son of Welf I, Duke of Bavaria. As a young man, he administered the family's property south of the Alps. Through his marriage to Wulfhild, daughter of Magnus, Duke of Saxony, he acquired part of the Billung pr
2 CONC operty in Saxony.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1116, he joined Emperor Henry V's Italian campaign. He succeeded his brother Welf II, Duke of Bavaria, when the latter died childless in 1120.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the royal election of 1125, he supported his son-in-law Frederick II, Duke of Swabia, but switched his allegiance to Lothair, Duke of Saxony, after Lothair promised that Gertrud, his only daughter and heir, would marry Henry's 
2 CONC son Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Lothair won the election and banned Frederick, in 1126 Henry abdicated as duke of Bavaria and retired to the family foundation of Weingarten Abbey so that he did not have to take part in the prosecution of his son-in-law. He
2 CONC nry died shortly thereafter and was buried in Weingarten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Judith, married Frederick II, Duke of Swabia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Conrad, died 17 March 1126
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry X the Proud
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Welf
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Sophia, married Berthold III, Duke of Zähringen and Leopold I, Duke of Styria
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Wulfhild, married Rudolf, Count of Bregenz
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mathilde, married Diepold IV, Margrave of Vohburg and Gebhard III, Count of Sulzbach
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Adalbert, Abbot of Corvey
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT      He gained the title of Herzog von Sachsen auf der Elbe. Heinrich IX Herzog von Bayern also went by the nick-name of Heinrich 'the Black'. He succeeded as the Herzog von Bayern in 1120
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Literatur'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernd Schneidmüller: Die Welfen. Herrschaft und Erinnerung (819–1252) (= Urban-Taschenbücher 465). Kohlhammer, Stuttgart u. a. 2000, ISBN 3-17-014999-7, S. 149 ff.
2 CONT Sigmund Ritter von Riezler: Heinrich IX. In: Allgemeine Deutsche Biographie (ADB). Band 11, Duncker & Humblot, Leipzig 1880, S. 461 f.
2 CONT Kurt Reindel: Heinrich IX. der Schwarze. In: Neue Deutsche Biographie (NDB). Band 8, Duncker & Humblot, Berlin 1969, ISBN 3-428-00189-3, S. 343
2 CONT Knut Görich: Die Staufer. Herrscher und Reich (= Becksche Reihe 2393). Beck, München 2006, ISBN 3-406-53593-3, S. 26.
2 CONT Georg Voss: Großherzogthum Sachsen-Weimar-Eisenach: Verwaltungsbezirk Eisenach: Amtsgerichtsbezirk Eisenach – die Wartburg, Jena 1917, S. 381: Gemälde des 16. Jhd. Heinrich der Welph, mit Anmerkungen zu weiteren Darstellungen, die
2 CONC  ihn ebenso bezeichnen. 
2 CONT Johann Agricola: Warhafftige Abcontrafactur und Bildnis der Groß-Hertzogen auch Chur und Fürsten, Dresden 1608, Nr. 11: Von Gottes Gnaden Hertzog Heinrich der Welff.
