1 NOTE Baldwin IV &quot;the Bearded&quot;
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=b745b404-1fdc-4ca8-b1b5-b73c2200a089&tid=12140672&pid=-107746351
1 NOTE     Baldwin IV of Flanders, known as the Bearded, was count of Flanders from 988 to 1037.
2 CONT     He was the son of Arnulf II of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Baldwin turned his attentions to the east and north, leaving the southern part of his territory in the hands of his vassals the counts of Guines, Hesdin, and St. Pol.
2 CONT
2 CONT     To the east was Lotharingia, and here Baldwin took Valenciennes, the Cambresis, and Hainaut. It was not until 1056, during the minority of the Emperor Henry IV, then he fully secured this territory, which was then recognized a
2 CONC s fier held of the emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT     In the more central and northerly parts of Flanders, the counts supremacy was unchallenged. Here there was a great deal of internal colonization of marshland, all of which belonged to the counts of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin first married Ogive of Luxemburg, and was succeeded by their son Baldwin V. He later married Eleanor of Normandy, daughter of Richard II of Normandy, by whom he had a daughter Judith. She married first Tostig Godwinson, Ea
2 CONC rl of Northumberland, and then Duke Welf of Bavaria. These widespread family connections demonstrate the political interests of the Flemish counts, both in England to the west and in Germany to the east.
2 CONT
2 CONT     1Signe Elisabeth Zijdemans (SEZ), Ahnentafel of Karen Kristine Fredriksdtr Nuland (73501), Signe Elisabeth Zijdemans, Åsnes 4400 Flekkefjord.
2 CONT     Sent to Ken Larson in an Email on 15 Mar 2002. Source noted as from the Flekkefjord History group.
2 CONT
