2 CONT
2 CONT Harold Godwinson, or Harold II (c. 1022 – October 14, 1066) was the last of the Anglo-Saxons to be crowned King of England - Edgar Ætheling (c. 1051 – c. 1126) was to be his successor after the Battle of Hastings, by the proclaima
2 CONC tion of the Witan, but was not crowned. His reign was from January 5 to October 14, 1066. His death was at the Battle of Hastings, by the lances of Norman knights under William the Conqueror.
2 CONT
