1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Erlend Ølvesson from Gjerde=
2 CONT
2 CONT '' 'Lendemann and large farmer on Gjerde gnr 9/1, Etne, Hordaland' ''
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was the son of Ølve at Studla, The mother is unknown
2 CONT * Erlend was married to Borghild Gudbrandsdotter, they had a son Sven
2 CONT * Erlend one of the men to whom King Olav Haraldsson connected and gave power in his first years of government.
2 CONT * Erlend later turned against the king, and this was probably what the king betrayed when he spoke to those who were against him before the battle of Stiklestad. He put it this way: "I made you, small as you were, into a great man
2 CONC ."
2 CONT * Erlend was one of the farmers' leaders in the battle of Stiklestad
2 CONT * Both Erlend from Gjerde and Aslak from Finnøy fell in the battle of Stiklestad in 1030
2 CONT * In the cemetery at Gjerde there is still a high monument with a cross high at the top. Several researchers believe that the stone was erected in memory of Erlend from Gjerde.
2 CONT * Erland på Gärdet, born in the 10th century; A rich Länsman (Länsherre) in Norway at the year 1020. About him and his descendants, next to King Magnus Erlingsson, see in von Dalins Historia, del. 2, chap. 5, § 9 in not. and in St
2 CONC urlesson, Tom. 1. 
2 CONT * [http://runeberg.org/anrep/3/0375.html '''von Nackreij - Skytte, Volume 3, page 371''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Etymology: Norse Stuðla Stødle Family=
2 CONT
2 CONT Etymology: Norse Stuðla Stødle family, Norwegian nobility from the Middle Ages, named after the farm Stødle (now Støle) in Etne, Sunnhordland. The family descended from Erlend av Gerde (Gjerde in Etne), who was one of the farmers'
2 CONC  leaders in the battle of Stiklestad 1030. Erlend's grandson's son was the employed lieutenant Orm Sveinsson (Kyrpinga-Orm). Orm's son Erling (Skakke) married Sigurd Jorsalfare's daughter Kristine, and was the father of King Magnu
2 CONC s Erlingsson. Both Kyrpinga-Orm and Erling Skakke lived in Stødle.
2 CONT
