2 CONT '''BENGT Folkason "Snivel", son of FOLKE "den digre/the Fat" Jarl in Sweden & his wife Ingegerd of Denmark''' (-bur [Varnhem Abbey]).  Saxo Grammaticus names Ingegerd's sons Knud and Bengt[9].  '''Jarl in Sweden.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Bengt & his wife had three children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.     '''BIRGER "Brosa''' (-9 Jan 1202).  He is named as the son of Bengt in the 14th century Varnem Abbey genealogy[10].  Jarl in Sweden 1174.  “Byrgerus dux magnus et Karolus fratres eius” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/8
2 CONC 5] under which “Kanutus…Rex Sweorum atque Gotthorum” donated property to the monks of Juleta kloster[11].  “…B. dux…M. frater ducis B et filius eius Eskillus…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “Kanutus…Sweorum re
2 CONC x” donated property to the monks of Juleta kloster[12].  “Byrgo Sweorum et Guttorum dux…Philippus frater meus, Magnus et Karolus fratres ducis…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “K…Sweorum rex filius Herjcjs itjd
2 CONC em regis” donated property to Nydala kloster[13].  The Saga of King Sverre records the death of "Earl Birgi Brosa" in the same year as Sverre King of Norway[14].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1202 of "Birgerus comes in
2 CONC  Suecia"[15].  m (after 1161) as her third husband, '''BRIGIDA of Norway,''' widow firstly of KARL Sunasson Jarl in Västergötland, and secondly of MAGNUS Henriksson, King in Östergötland, daughter of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway 
2 CONC & his [first/second] wife --- (-[Riseberga Abbey] 22 Oct.  Snorre records that "King Harald Gille's daughter Brigida" was first married to "the Swedish king Inge Halsteinson, and afterwards to Earl Karl Sonason, and then to the Sw
2 CONC edish king Magnus", noting that she and King Inge Haraldson were cousins by the mother's side, and "at last [she] married Earl Birger Brose"[16].  It is not chronologically possible for Brigida to have married Inge Halsteinson Kin
2 CONC g of Sweden, who died in 1118.  She must have been an infant at the time of her marriage to Karl Sunasson.  The Saga of King Sverre records that "Earl Birgi Brossa" had married "Brigit", the sister of King Sverre's father[17].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger & his wife Brigida of Norway had seven children''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''FILIP Birgersson''' (-killed in battle [Akerhus] 4 Jan 1200).  Snorre names (in order) "Earl Philip, Earl Knut, Folke and Magnus" as the four sons of "Earl Birger Brose" & his wife[18].  Jarl in Sweden.  The Saga o
2 CONC f King Sverre names "Philippus son of Earl Birgi" at a meeting of the Birkibeins at Borg[19].  The Saga of King Sverre records that "Earl Philippus " was killed by the Bagels at Oslo[20].
2 CONT
