2 CONT Canute I of Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute I Eriksson (Old Norse: Knútr Eiríksson) or Knut Eriksson in modern Swedish (born before 1150 - died 1195/96) was king over all of Sweden from 1173 to 1195 (rival king since 1167). He was a son of king Eric the Saint and Kri
2 CONC stina (probably a granddaughter of Inge the Elder.
2 CONT
2 CONT After killing Charles Sverkerson in 1167, Canut, who had just returned home after ten years in exile, started fighting for power against Sverker the Elder's sons Kol and Boleslaw Sverkerson. Only in 1173 could he call himself king
2 CONC  of the whole country.
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute's able jarl from 1174 was Birger Brosa (died in 1202)
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute built a castle on the island of Stockholm in 1187, one of many such fortifications made necessary by heathen incursions from the Baltic lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT Skáldatal names two of Knut Eriksson's skalds: Hallbjörn hali and Þorsteinn Þorbjarnarson.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Married around 1160, name of his wife is unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon Knutsson (slain November 1205 at Älgarås)
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Knutsson (slain November 1205 at Älgarås)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joar Knutsson (slain November 1205 at Älgarås)
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Knutsson, who would defeat Sverker the Younger and become King of Sweden in 1208.
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter, NN Knutsdotter (possibly Sigrid, or Karin), who is said to have married either jarl Knut Birgersson (and become mother of Magnus Broka), or married Magnus Broka himself (and with Magnus had a son Knut Magnusson, or, Knut
2 CONC  Katarinason, claimant of Swedish throne and killed in 1251). Existence of this daughter is based on unclear mentions in old saga and chronicle material, and is to an extent accepted in research literature, to explicate Knut Magnu
2 CONC sson's hereditary claim to the throne. This daughter was by necessity born in 1170s or 1180s. She is also proposed by old romantical-looking genealogies as mother of a Duke's daughter Cecilia Knutsdotter (by necessity born near 12
2 CONC 08 at earliest), whose parentage however is fully shrouded in mists of history.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Knut Eriksson, d. 1195 eller 1196. Kung av Sverige från 1167. Son till Erik den helige. Knut vistades i landsflykt i Norge några år efter faderns död, men övertog kungatiteln 1167 efter att ha dödat företrädaren Karl Sverkersson p
2 CONC å Näs, Visingsö, bl asom hämnd för mordet på fadern. Dennes brorsöner Burislev och Kol har dock uppträtt som tronpretendenter men även dessa dödades av Knut. Tillsammans med jarlen Birger Brosa ingick Knut en handelstraktat med he
2 CONC rtig Henrik Lejonet av Sachsen. Under Knuts tid förekom en omfattande myntning och han har utfärdat de äldsta bevarade breven av en svensk kung. Uppgifter finns om att han förde krig mot hedningar på andra sidan Östersjön. Knut ha
2 CONC de goda förbindelser med kung Sverre av Norge men mer spända relationer med danska kungar. Han dog en naturlig död och begravdes i Varnhems kloster. Källa: "Nationalencyklopedin"
2 CONT
2 CONT Enl Jäderlund gift med Ingeborg af Danmark.
2 CONT
