1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Queen Ulvhild Haakonsdotter, of Aalborg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Håkon Finnson av Tjøtta and Brigid Ulfsdatter 
2 CONT * Ulvhild Håkonsdatter (born about 1095, died 1148) was the queen of Sweden in the 12th century , who was strongly involved in Nordic great power politics, among other things it was claimed that she was a poison killer and a stron
2 CONC g-willed intriguer.
2 CONT * Ulfhild was the queen of Sweden and Denmark, reign 1117–1125, at the same time with Ingegerd Haraldsdotter until 1118
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulvhild was married three times, with three different kings: Her first two marriages were childless. After King Nil's death, Ulvhild left Denmark for Sweden (some sources indicate that she made herself impossible in Denmark and le
2 CONC ft him before). She convinced the East Gothic chief Sverker that he would have greater prospects of being accepted even in Västergötland if he took her to wife, which also happened; In 1130, Sverker was celebrated as the entire Ki
2 CONC ng of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married '''(1) INGE II King of Sweden''' (-[1125]).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He succeeded as INGE II King of Sweden.  After his death, Magnus Nielsson of Denmark was chosen a
2 CONC s king of Sweden [Västergötland] in 1129[89].  married firstly RAGNHILD, daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  St Ragnhild of Telje is identified in some sources as queen of
2 CONC  King Inge II[90].  married secondly as her first husband, ULVHILD Haakonsdotter, daughter of HAAKON Finsson & his wife --- (-before 1143). 
2 CONT * Married '''(2) Nils of Denmark''' married secondly (divorced) as her second husband, ULVHILD Haakonsdotter, widow of INGE II Halstensson King of Sweden, daughter of HAAKON Finsson & his wife --- (-before 1143).
2 CONT * Married '''(3)  Sverker the older''' Her second marriage is referred to by Saxo Grammaticus.  She was secretly abducted by Sverker I King of Sweden but their "connection was accepted as a marriage".
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#SverkerIdied1156B Project MedLands Sweden]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Sverker I & his first [wife] had four children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''JOHAN Sverkersson''' (-murdered [1153/54]).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He appears to have been his father's designated heir but was killed (by peasants?) some yea
2 CONC rs before his father's death[128].   
2 CONT * 2.         '''KARL Sverkersson''' (-murdered Visingsö 12 Apr [1166], bur Alvastra Abbey).  His parentage is stated by Saxo Grammaticus[129].  He succeeded in 1161 as KARL I King of Sweden.  '''married (1163) KRISTIN Stigsdatter 
2 CONC [Hvide], daughter of STIG Tokesen "Hvitaleder/White leather" [Hvide] & his wife Margrete Knudsdatter of Denmark.''' Snorre names (in order) "the Danish king Valdemar…and daughters Margaret, Christina and Catherine" as the children
2 CONC  of "Canute Lavard" & his wife, recording that Margrete married "Stig Hvitaled" and that their daughter was "Christina, married to the Swedish king, Karl Sorkvison, and their son was king Sorkver"[130].  Fagrskinna names (in order
2 CONC ) “Valdimarr konungr ok Kristin ok Katerin or Margareta” as children of “Knútr lávardr, bródir Eiriks eimuna” and his wife, noting that Margrete married “Stigr hvitaledr”, father of “Nikoláss ok Kristinar er átti Karl konungr Sver
2 CONC kissunr”[131].  Morkinskinna records that “Karl Sørkvisson king of the Swedes” married “Kristín daughter of “Stígr hvítaledr” and his wife Margret[132].
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' King Karl & his wife Kristín Stigsdatter had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''SVERKER Karlson''' (-killed in battle Gestilren 17 Jul 1210, bur Alvastra Abbey).  Snorre names "king Sorkver" as son of "the Swedish king, Karl Sorkvison" & his wife[133].  Fagrskinna names “Sverkir konungr, f
2 CONC adir Jóans konungs” as son of “Kristinar er átti Karl konungr Sverkissunr”[134].  He succeeded in 1196 as SVERKER II "den yngre/the younger" King of Sweden.  The Saga of King Sverre records the accession of "Sorkvi Karlsson" after
2 CONC  the death of "King Knut of Sweden"[135].  “Swerco filius Karoli Regis rex Sweorum” donated property to the monks of Nydala by charter dated to [1196/1210][136].  The Icelandic Annals record the battle in 1208 between "Svercherum 
2 CONC Caroli filius" and "Ericum Canuti filium, Suecorum reges"[137].  Deposed 1208.  '''married firstly BENGTE Ebbesdatter [Galen], daughter of EBBE Sunesen [Galen] from Knardrup & his wife''' ---.  The primary source which confirms he
2 CONC r parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  '''married secondly INGEGÄRD Birgersdotter, daughter of BIRGER Bengtsson "Brosa" Jarl in Sweden & his wife Brigida of Norway (-after 1210).'''  Snorre names (in order) "Ingege
2 CONC rd…married to the Swedish king Sorkver [and] a second daughter…Kristin and a third Margaret" as the daughters of "Earl Birger Brose" & his wife[138].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Sverker II & his first wife BENGTE Ebbesdatter had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* i)          '''KARL Sverkersson''' (-murdered in the mountains near Trondheim 1198).  The Saga of King Sverre records the marriage of "Karl son of King Sorkvi" and "Ingibiorg daughter of King Sverri"[139].  m INGEBORG Sver
2 CONC resdatter of Norway, daughter of SVERRE King of Norway & his first wife Astrid Rösdatter.
2 CONT >>>>>>* ii)         '''HELENA Sverkersdotter''' (-after 1240).  A charter dated 1237 refers to the marriage of “S. Fulconis ducis filius” and “E. Suerchonis Regis filia” after her abduction from Vreta convent[140].  m (before 1237
2 CONC ) SUNE Folkason Jarl in Sweden, son of FOLKER Birgersson [Folkunge] Jarl in Sweden & his wife (-1247). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Sverker II & his second wife INGEGÄRD Birgersdotter had [two] children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* iii)        '''KARL Sverkersson''' (-1213).  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1213 of "Carolus Svercheri filius"[141].  If King Sverker was his father, Karl must have been from the king´s second marriage, after the
2 CONC  death of his older half-brother of the same name.] 
2 CONT >>>>>>* iv)       '''JOHAN Sverkersson''' (1201-Visingsö 10 Mar 1222, bur Alvastra Abbey).  Snorre names "King Jon" as the son of "the Swedish king Sorkver" and his wife Ingegerd[142].  Morkinskinna names “King Jón” as son of “Kin
2 CONC g Sørkvir”[143].  The Saga of King Sverre records the death of "Earl Birgi Brosa" in the same year as Sverre King of Norway [in 1202], commenting that "the Swedes then took Jon son of King Sorkvi…one year old"[144].  Fagrskinna na
2 CONC mes “Sverkir konungr, fadir Jóans konungs” as son of “Kristinar er átti Karl konungr Sverkissunr”[145].  He succeeded in 1216 as JOHAN I King of Sweden, crowned [1219].  The Icelandic Annals record the succession in 1216 of "Johan
2 CONC nes Svercheri filius" who reigned for six years[146].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1222 of "Johannes Sverkeri filus rex Suecorum"[147]. 
2 CONT * 3.         '''INGEGÄRD''' (-1172, bur Vreta Abbey).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m (1156) KNUD III Magnussen Joint King of Denmark, son of MAGNUS I "den Stærke/the S
2 CONC trong" King of Denmark & his wife Ryksa [Swantosława] of Poland ([1129]-murdered Roskilde 9 Aug 1157).
2 CONT * 4.         '''INGEGÄRD''' (-1204).  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  Prioress at Vretakloster 1164.
2 CONT
