1 OCCU Finländsk adelsdam. Länstagare av Viborgs län 1511-1513
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunilla_Bese '''Gunilla Johansdotter Bese'''], also called '''Gunhild''' (1475–1553) was a Finnish (Swedish) noble and ''fiefholder'' of Viipuri Castle from 1511 to 1513.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bese was the''' daughter of Johan Stensson Bese and Catherine Jonsdotter. She married riksråd [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Bielke Eric Bielke], fiefholder of Viipuri. After the death of her spouse in 1511, she took over 
2 CONC his position as interim governor and commandant of Viipuri until a new governor was appointed and installed in 1513.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During her term''', the peace treaty of 1510 was threatened by the Russians, but she issued renewed peace negotiations and thereby prevented the outbreak of a new war. In 1512, she opposed the suggested candidate for the positi
2 CONC on of commandant of Viipuri, and eventually succeeded in having her son-in-law, Lord Toni Eriksson Tott to replace her; she ceded her position to him in 1513. After this, she retired to tend to the estates left to her by her late 
2 CONC spouse in Sweden, and was described as an efficient landowner.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1520 at''' Kalmar Castle, Bese's eldest daughter [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_Bielke Anna] had a similar experience to her mother's; when Anna's husband, the governor, died, she continued to rule the castle and fief a
2 CONC nd led the war efforts (in that case, against the Danish). Her son Axel's descendant [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunilla_Bielke Gunilla Bielke] became queen, the second wife of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_III_of_Sweden 
2 CONC John III of Sweden].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bese died on''' 7 April 1553 in Bernhamra, Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Legacy===
2 CONT
2 CONT The [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fru_Gunillas_Gr%C3%A4nd Fru Gunillas Gränd] in Stockholm is named after her.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 	Finländsk adelsdam. Länstagare av Viborgs län 1511-1513.
