1 OCCU Riddare, Riksråd och Hövidsman Älfsborg Tofta och Eriksstad
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Gustaf Olsson Stenbock, till Toftaholm=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Olof Johansson (Stenbock).
2 CONT * Gustaf Olofsson to Toftaholm ( Gustaf Olofsson Stenbock the Elder ), dead in the 1490s (before 1493), the son of Olof Johansson (Stenbock), was the Swedish national council and politician during the time of the Kalmar Union . Wi
2 CONC th him, the older Capricorn extinct .
2 CONT * He was the chief white man at Älvsborg during the battles between Karl Knutsson and Kristian I in 1452. He got Sunnerbo hardened in the course of Kristian, but during Sten Sture the elder he stood on his side.
2 CONT * The Council of Ministers and politicians during the Union period. Hövitsman at Älfsborg during the battles between Karl Knutsson and Kristian 1452. Got Sunnerbo hardened in the lecture by Kristian II. During Sten Sture's time he
2 CONC  stood on his side.
2 CONT * Gustav Olofsson to Toftaholm, national council and politician during the Union period
2 CONT * Knights, national council and Hövitsman
2 CONT * He was known twice as married, first with Ingrid Bengtsdotter (Vinstorpaätten) and then with Anna Turesdotter (Bielke). With either of his wives he got his daughter Anna, who was married to the Swedish National Council Arvid Knu
2 CONC tsson to Torpa in Västergötland. Their son Olof took up his arms of the mother-of-exile and became an ancestor of the younger Capricorn family.
2 CONT
2 CONT * No male descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Stenbock,_%C3%A4ldre_%C3%A4tten#TAB_4 Capricorn, Older Family]
2 CONT
2 CONT The above modern designation goes back to the fact that the family, which since the latter half of the 16th century bore the name Stenbock after its coat of arms, has taken up this coat of arms from the present already extinct 149
2 CONC 2 on the man's side, from which it derives from the mother. Originally, the family belonged to the low-farmer in the Småland province of Finnveden. Its oldest known ancestor's son, however, became the council during the rebellion 
2 CONC of the 1430s and father of two councils, one of which was active in Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustav Olsson(son of Olof Jönsson). Mentioned at the earliest 1441. Was knighted between 28.3 1448 and 17.3 1450, thus at the coronation of King Karl Knutsson either in Uppsala 29.6 1448 or in Trondheim 20.11 1449. Was 1452 chief 
2 CONC white man at Älvsborg, where a salvo letter to him was already dated 17.3 1450, and contained 1454 as well Älvsborg and Lödöse as Örebro castle and town but were so removed. or 1455 Älvsborg by the Norwegian knight Olof Nilsson (S
2 CONC kanke) on behalf of Kristian I. Became at the last council in 1463, which he was still 20.2 1488 and apparently still 1489. Supposed to have been a layman in Tiohärad 1464 and 1473. Received as a lecture by King Kristian probably 
2 CONC Allbo hd in Småland and by the national council for life 31.1 1465 Sunnerbo hd in the same landscape, which loan 26.11 1483 was increased with Västbo hd in the same landscape. His seat was 1466 Erikstad in Vittaryds sn in Sunnerbo
2 CONC  but 20.3 1477 and still 13.1 1482 Tofta in Dörarps sn, the same hd. Died between 3.5 and 18.10 1492.Gave 2.6 1488 Erikstad in Vittaryds snow and other land in Sunnerbo hd as a morning gift to his later wife Anna Turedotter, who, 
2 CONC as a widow, dated letters to Erikstad and is said to have died there 23.4 1513, daughter of the knight, the council and the lawman Ture Tureson ( Bielke ), whose only known wife was Ingegärd Kymingsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Married: (1)  between 1445 and 1448 with '''Ingrid Bengtsdotter,''' who was a widow of the knight Tomas Bengtsson (Pipa ) in Bysta in Askers sn and hd in Närke, died in 1484 and was the daughter of the National Council Bengt Ud
2 CONC dsson ( Vinstorpaätten ) and Kristina Staffansdotter ( Ulv ).  Gave 2.6 1488 Erikstad in Vittaryds snow and other land in Sunnerbo hd as a morning gift to his later wife Anna Turedotter, who, as a widow, dated letters to Erikstad 
2 CONC and is said to have died there 23.4 1513, daughter of the knight, the council and the lawman Ture Tureson ( Bielke ), whose only known wife was Ingegärd Kymingsdotter.
2 CONT * Married: '''Anna Turesdotter''', died 1513-04-23 at Erikstad (Bbl.) In Vittaryds parish, Kronoberg County. Married 1488-06-01 Toftaholm (Bbl.) With the knight, the national council and the governor of Älvsborg Gustaf Olofsson (o
2 CONC f old Stenbocks genealogy), to Tofta, Erikstad and Kälunda, in his 2nd marriage, died in 1494.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Ingrid Bengtsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Anna Gustavsdotter (Stenbock),''' was married to the Swedish National Council Arvid Knutsson to Torpa in Västergötland. Their son Olof Arvidsson (Stenbock) took up his arms of the mother-of-kin that had expired and became an 
2 CONC ancestor of the younger Stenbock family. With Gustaf Olofsson (Stenbock) d.i. extinct the older Capricorn species.  'Anna Gustavsdotter (Stenbock) received  in 1488 Tofta in Dörarps sn, Sunnerbo hd in Småland by the father. Died n
2 CONC o later than 27.2 or 24.9 1508. - Received 12.9 1474 the Lidhem farm in Väckelsångs sn, Konga hd in Småland and land in this as well as Allbo, Norrvidinge and Sunnerbo hd in the same landscape as morning gift by the knight Ficke G
2 CONC ustavsson ( Ängätten ), which is not later mentioned in life. 25.8 1477 she received the Torpa farm in Länghems sn. Kinds hd in Västergötland along with land in this and As hd in the same landscape and in Västbo hd in Småland as a
2 CONC  morning gift by the lawman in Tiohärad, later the national council and the governor of Kind Arvid Knutsson ( save over star ), which was joined in Kalmar at least 1474-1481 , at his death, was a chief white man on Öresten in Väst
2 CONC ergötland and died between 12.3 1497 and 25.3 1498.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source'''  Capricorn, older family 
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned at the earliest 1441. Was knighted between 28/3 1448 and 17/3 1450. Was Hövitsman at Älvsborg where a sales letter to him was already dated 17/3 1450 and held 1454 Älvsborg and Lödöse, Örebro castle and town but was remo
2 CONC ved the same year or 1455 Älvsborg by the Norwegian knight Olof Nilsson Skanke on behalf of Kristian I.
2 CONT Became the national council in 1463 and was there until 20/2 1488, Was lawman in Tiohärad 1464 and 1473. Received as a lecture by King Kristian I. Allbo hd in Småland and by the national council for life 31/1 1465 Sunnerbo hd in S
2 CONC måland, 26/11 1483 with Västbo hd in Småland. His seat was 1466 Erikstad in Vittaryds sn in Sunnerbo but 20/3 1477 and still 31/1 1482 Tofta in Dörarps sn in the same hd, which he called Toftaholm. At this site there was during th
2 CONC e Middle Ages the village of Tofta consisting of eight homesteads, Gustav bought all of them and in the late 1400s built a fortified house on the present so-called. Stenhus or Körsbärsholmen. Ruins of this remain. The house itself
2 CONC  was walled with cobblestones, 23 meters long and 10 meters wide. It was surrounded by a stone wall, and at the northern tip of the islet there are remains of the bridge that in its time connected the islet with the mainland. Also
2 CONC  owned land in Sunnerbo, Västbo, Östbo, Tveta, Vista and Västra hd in Småland. Heaven hd in Halland. Kullings, Vadsbo, Vartofta and Viste hd in Västergötland. Lösings and Ydre hd in Östergötland. Askers and Grimsten's hd in Närke.
2 CONC  Norunda and Ulleråkers hd in Uppland. Skåne and Slangerup in Zealand.
2 CONT
