1 OCCU Comte, de Werl, d'Arnsberg, NKG XI-202, Graf von Werl-Arnsberg, erbaut um 1072 Burg Arnsberg, Graf von Werl-Arnsberg und Vogt des Bistums Paderborn., Reichsministerialer in der Wetterau (Hessen)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konrad_II._(Werl-Arnsberg)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ''from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXON%20NOBILITY.htm#KonradWerldied1092 v4.1 Updated 03 November 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT '''KONRAD von Werl''', son of BERNHARD Graf von Werl[-Arnsberg] & his wife --- (-killed in battle Friesland 10 Jul 1092).  Graf von Werl[-Arnsberg].  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Vo
2 CONC gt of Paderborn Cathedral 1066.  He was killed fighting the Frisians in 1092[1951].  The Annales Corbeienses record that "Counradus comes" was killed "a Morsaciensibus" in 1092[1952]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m MATHILDE von Northeim, daughter of OTTO I Graf von Northeim Duke of Bavaria & his wife Richenza [Ezzonen].  The Annalista Saxo names "Heinricum Crassum comitem…Sifridum de Boumeneburh et Cononem comitem de Bichlinge et tres fili
2 CONC as, terciam vero duxit Conradus comes de Arnesberge" as children of Otto von Northeim & his wife[1953].  The Annales Stadenses also refers to the four daughters of Otto, specifying that "secunda mater fuit Frederici comitis de Arn
2 CONC esberch" but does not name her[1954].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Konrad & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HERMANN von Werl (-killed in battle 19 Jul 1092).  <br/>
2 CONT 2.         FRIEDRICH "der Streitbare" von Werl (-11 Feb 1124).  <br/>
2 CONT 3.         HEINRICH von Werl (-[1115/18]).<br/>
