2 CONT 2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Fulk-III-the-Black-count-of-Anjou-Vend%C3%B4me/6000000000222677079?through=6000000009909505293 FOULQUES] d'Anjou ([970]-Metz 21 Jun 1040, bur Beaulieu-lez-Loche, Abbaye de Saint-Pierre).  Th
2 CONC e Historiæ Andegavensis, allegedly written by Foulques IV "Rechin" Comte d'Anjou, names "Goffridus Grisagonella pater avi mei Fulconis"[104].  He succeeded his father in 987 as FOULQUES III "Nerra/the Black" Comte d'Anjou. 
