2 CONC o withstood a peasant insurrection, and helped the King Robert II of France against the Duchy of Burgundy. It also repelled an attack on English on the peninsula of Cotentin , which was led by Ethelred II of England. Also pursued 
2 CONC a reform of the monasteries Normans. Ricardo tried to improve relations with England through the marriage of his sister Emma to King Ethelred, but she disliked the British. Anyway, this connection meant later one of the reasons sh
2 CONC e used her grandson William the Conqueror to claim the throne of England. In 996 he married Judith of Brittany (982-1017), daughter of Conan I, Duke of Brittany. Her offspring was as follows: Ricardo (997-1027), Duke of Normandy i
2 CONC n 1027, the son of her grandmother Adelaide (b. 1003 / 5), married to Reginald I, Count of Burgundy Robert (c. 1005-1035), Duke of Normandy between 1027 and 1035 William (1007/9-1025), a monk of Fecamp Leonor (1011/3-1071), marrie
