1 NOTE Duke of Normandy
2 CONT Called Magnificent or Devil
2 CONT Book of Rememberence-Meacham
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestral Line back to Adam comes from the Genealogical Society of Utah Library Chart No. 30397, October 1945 "Kinship of Families"  by Archibald F. Bennett and from the records of Janet "Nettie" Sims and Ellen Anderson Mecham.
1 NOTE !BOOK: PEDIGREE OF SOME OF THE EMPEROR CHARLEMAGNE DESCENDANTS by Marcellus Donald A R Von Redlich
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 82-6
2 CONT From: Encyclopedia Britannica, Online, article: Robert I:
2 CONT
2 CONT " byname ROBERT THE MAGNIFICENT, OR THE DEVIL, French ROBERT LEMAGNIFIQUE, OR LE DIABLE, duke of Normandy (1027-35), the younger sonof Richard II of Normandy and the father, by his mistress Arlette, ofWilliam the Conqueror of Engl
2 CONC and. On the death of his father(1026/27), Robert contested the duchy with his elder brother RichardIII, legally the heir, until the latter's opportune death a few yearslater. A strong ruler, Robert succeeded in exacting the obedie
2 CONC nce ofhis vassals. On the death of Robert II the Pious, king of France(1031), a crisis arose over the succession to the French throne. TheDuke gave his support to Henry I against the party favouring hisyounger brother; in reward f
2 CONC or his services he demanded and receivedthe Vexin Fran?cais, a territory not far north of Paris. A patron ofthe monastic reform movement, he died while returning from apilgrimage to Jerusalem."
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT     1. Tab. Souv. Gen., France 22, Tab. 32, 48
2 CONT     2. Dukes of Normandy, France 5, p. 115-27
2 CONT     3. Keiser und Koenig Hist., Gen. Hist. 25, pt 1, p. 100-01
2 CONT     4. Burke's Peerage, Eng. P, 1949, pref. p. 252
2 CONT
2 CONT !RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT     1. Though Robert I never married Harlette according to Norman law or custon,he was faithful to her and she to him until his death.
1 NOTE 6th Duke d'Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Bastard son of Richard II.
1 NOTE 6th Duke d'Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Bastard son of Richard II.
