2 CONT 1.      '''   ADELAIS''' [Judith] ([1000]-7 Jul [after 1030]).  Guillaume of Jumièges names “Adeliz” as the first daughter of “dux Richardus” and his wife “Goiffredum Britannorum comitem...sororem...Iudith”, adding that she marrie
2 CONC d “Rainaldo Burgundionum comiti” by whom she had “Willelmum et Widonem” (the marriage is recorded in a later passage)[188].  Orderic Vitalis records her marriage and calls her amita of William I King of England[189].  "Otto comes 
2 CONC qui nominatur Willelmus" issued a charter dated 2 Nov 1023 subscribed by "Raynardi comitis, Adheleydis uxoris eius"[190].  "Raynaldi comitis, Adheleys uxoris eius" subscribed the charter dated 1030 by which "Robertus regis Roberti
2 CONC  filius et regis Henrici filii eius germanus…Burgundie Dux" restored property to Cluny[191].  ["Raginaldus comes comitis Guillelmi filius" donated property to the abbey of Flavigny by charter dated 18 May 1037 subscribed by "Iudid
2 CONC  comitisse uxoris eius, Guillelmi filii eius, Hugonis filii eius…"[192].  "Iudid comitisse" is assumed in traditional genealogies[193] to have been the same person as Adelais.  However, it is also possible that she was Comte Renau
2 CONC d's second wife, Adelais having died earlier.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 1 Sep 1016) [as his first wife,] RENAUD de Mâcon, son of OTHON GUILLAUME Comte de Mâcon [ Bourgogne-Comté ]  & his first wife Ermentrude de Roucy ([990]-3/4 Sep 1057, bur Besançon).  He succeeded his father in 1026
2 CONC  as RENAUD I Comte de Bourgogne. 
2 CONT
