2 CONT m [firstly] (before 1 Sep 1016) ADELAIS de Normandie, daughter of RICHARD II Duke of Normandy & his first wife Judith de Rennes [Bretagne] ([1000]-7 Jul [after 1030]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT [m secondly '''JUDITH, daughter of --- (-after 18 May 1037). ''' "Raginaldus comes comitis Guillelmi filius" donated property to the abbey of Flavigny by charter dated 18 May 1037 subscribed by "Iudid comitisse uxoris eius, Guille
2 CONC lmi filii eius, Hugonis filii eius…"[22].  "Iudid comitisse" is assumed in traditional genealogies[23] to have been the same person as Adelais.  However, it is also possible that she was Comte Renaud's second wife, Adelais having 
2 CONC died earlier.  This may be corroborated by Renaud's sons being described in the charter as "filii eius" rather than "filii eorum", although the use of these two grammatical variants is inconsistent in contemporary sources.]  
2 CONT
