2 CONT His ancestry is found elsewhere in this tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sparkalägg's father was Styrbjorn (The Strong) Olafsson and his mother was Queen of Norway Thyra Haraldsdottir.  His paternal grandparents were King of Sweden Olof (Mitkg) Bjornsson and Ingeberg Thrandsdottir; his maternal grandpa
2 CONC rents were Harald (Bluetooth) Gormsson of Denmark II and Gunnhild Olafsdottir
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile cannot be correct. 
2 CONT Torgils's death is noted with accuracy "22. September 1027". The date may well be correct, but if so, the circumstances surrounding it and his place of death is very wrong! There is only one "Battle of Svolder" in scandinavian his
2 CONC tory. This took place in 999 or 1000, ref. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Svolder. 
2 CONT It is not known for sure where "Svolder" was - it's assumed to be in the "western baltic" or in what is now danish coastal territory - however, assigning the location of Svolder to norwegian territory must be wrong. Olav Tryggvaso
2 CONC n was in effect "ambushed" at sea on a journy from "Vendland" (Pommerania) to Norway by the king of Denmark and the king of Sweden. That kind of attack you make close to your own stronhold. 
2 CONT Sweden at that time did not have a "west coast" to speak of. What is now western Sweden was either Denmark or Norway (south to what is now Gothenburg). 
2 CONT So, when Torgils was buried it was most probably in Denmark (Halland or Skåne which today are swedish territories). 
2 CONT
