2 CONT Torkel Styrbjörnsson, Torgils, Sprakalägg or Sprakling was the son of the disinherited Swedish prince Styrbjörn Starke, the son of king Olof (II) Björnsson of Sweden. His mother was Tyra, the daughter of Harold Bluetooth (king
2 CONC  of Denmark and Norway).
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at the Battle of Swold.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT Ulf Sprakaläggsson (988-1027), the Jarl of Canute the Great in Denmark and Danish steward. 
2 CONT Gytha Thorkelsdóttir who was to marry Godwin, Earl of Wessex.
2 CONT
