1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''Gregorius Dagsson'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT Lendmann Gregorius Jonson of Blind Heims Ætta in Sunnmøre
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Dag Eilivsson Bratsberg and Ragnhild Skoftedotter 
2 CONT * Gregorius Dagsson, D. 1161. He was an Ampman, owned and lived after his father in the great Bratsberg farm in Gjerpen. This farm received both the backrest and the Amt Bratsberg name after (Telemark County). Gregorius was the he
2 CONC ad of the great-man party who was under the contention between the sons of Harald Gille (d. 1136) and supported the best and least self-righteous of them, King Inge Krokrygg (d. 1161). During the fight, Bratsberg Gård was burned b
2 CONC y the brother of the King Eystein Haraldsson (d. 1157). Gregorius fell into battle with Eystein's son Håkon Herdebreid (d. 1162) near Kongshelle.
2 CONT * He was a lover, owned and lived after his father on the large farm Bratsberg in Gjerpen. This farm got both the lace and the county Bratsberg named after (Telemark county). Gregory was the leader of the Grand Duchy as under the 
2 CONC struggles between the sons of Harald Gille (d.1136) and supported the best and least self-righteous of them, King Inge Krokrygg (d.1161). During the fight, Bratsberg farm was burned by Inge's brother, King Eystein Haraldsson (d.11
2 CONC 57). Gregory fell in battle with Eystein's son Håkon Herdebreid (d.1162) near Kongshelle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://nbl.snl.no/Gregorius_Dagsson Gregorius Dagsson BY: Narve Bjørgo (University of Bergen)]
2 CONT
2 CONT THIS ARTICLE WAS PRINTED IN THE NORWEGIAN BIOGRAPHICAL LEXICON, WRITTEN BY: Narve Bjørgo (University of Bergen)
2 CONT
2 CONT Newer articles can be found in the large Norwegian encyclopedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lendmann. Parents: Lend The man day Eilivsson (sjto NBL1, Bd. 3) and Ragnhild Skoftesdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fact: DEAD January 7, 1161
2 CONT * PLACE OF DEATH Ranrike (no KUNGÄLV, Sweden), buried in Gimsøy, a convent at Skien
2 CONT * LIFETIME COMMENT Birth year and birthplace are unhereous
2 CONT * Birth year and birthplace are unhereous
2 CONT * Gregorius Dagsson was at the time in 1150, the dominant military and political tenant in the Krinsen broadcasting Inge Krokrygg (Inge 1 Haraldsson). A country-like aristocratic gathering of Inge seems to have also his superior's
2 CONC  political goals.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gregorius had close family and moon bands to the King's Ætta and to the multiple of the most powerful great man's genera in the country. Mora Ragnhild Skoftesdotter was the father of Giskeætta, and his maternal grandfather, and Mu
2 CONC ndsson, was the younger child of King Olav Haraldsson Kyrre. He was the foster-brother of King Inge Krokrygg, a man-in-law. Through the poison moon to the syrups of Borghild Dagdotter and Sigrid Dagdotter, Gregorius stood in the b
2 CONC rother-in-law of the Orcman's ætes at Austrått in Sør-Trøndelag and Vetteland in Ranrike. The Reformation and friendship relationships of this battle created the foundations of a party prega political interest fellowship between p
