1 TITL Prince of Ryazan
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Igor Glebovich''' (died in 1194) — prince of Ryazan. Participated in the battle on Koloksha river (1177).
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Gleb Rostislavich in a Vladimir prison in 1177, the Ryazan principality was left in the joint possession of Igor and his brothers Roman and Vladimir, and the Ryazan throne went to Roman as the eldest brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1180, Igor participated on the side of Roman in civil strife against the brothers Vladimir and Vsevolod, supported by Vsevolod the Big Nest. In 1186, the second Vladimir intervention in the Ryazan principality was successful du
2 CONC e to the struggle of Roman, Igor and Vladimir against Vsevolod and Svyatoslav, who owned the Principality of Pronsk. Vsevolod the Big Nest forced the restless Ryazan princes to kiss the cross "with all his will."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: Gleb Rostislavich (d. 1178) - Prince of Ryazan (1145-1177 intermittently).
2 CONT * Mother: Euphrosyne (Evfrosinya) Rostislavna (d. 1179) - daughter of Rostislav Yurievich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brothers and sisters:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Andrey (d. before 1186) - prince of Ryazan.
2 CONT * Roman (d. 1216) - prince of Ryazan 1180-1207.
2 CONT * Theodosia - married to Mstislav the Brave.
2 CONT * Vladimir (d. after 1186) - prince of Pronsk 1180-before 1186.
2 CONT * Vsevolod (d. 1207) - prince of Pronsk before 1186 and 1188-1207 and prince of  Kolomna 1186-1188.
2 CONT * Svyatoslav (d. after 1207) - Principal Prince of Pronsk.
2 CONT * Yaroslav (d. after 1199) - prince of Ryazan .
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Agrafena (d. 1237) - daughter of Rostislav Mstislavich (only if Yuri of Ryazan in 1237 was Igorevich, brother of Ingvar; if Yuri was Ingvarevich, then Agrafena is Ingvar's wife, and then it is even more doubtful that she is 
2 CONC the daughter of Rostislav Mstislavich of Smolensk ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Roman (d. 1217) - Principal Prince of Ryazan.
2 CONT # Ingvar (d. 1235) - prince of Ryazan 1217-1235.
2 CONT # Yuri (d. 1237) - presumably the Grand Duke of Ryazan 1235-1237.
