2 CONC  Goths Erik. The Earl of the Goths is likely to be connected with the Eriksberg royal estate in Gäsene, here in Västergötland, on which farm King Knut Eriksson, according to Vidhemsprästen, died in 1195 or 1196, after which he is 
2 CONC buried in Varnhem's monastery church. According to this arrangement, Lagman Eskil's name may be applied for in Lund, Archbishop Eskil. Furthermore, a close relationship could be demonstrated between the Erikska royal family and th
2 CONC e Folkungaätten. As stated in the text, the image of Eskil Magnusson as a descendant of the Gothic Earl Erik is disturbed by the fact that Magnus Minnesköld and an NN Karlsdotter would be siblings. Marriages between chieftains vio
2 CONC lated the rules of canon law, which could, however, be abolished by the Pope. However, it should be noted that one of Magnus Minnesköld's older sons is Bishop Karl Magnusson in Linköping, who could be named after his possible gran
2 CONC dfather Karl Eriksson.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' VÄSTERGÖTLANDS  Lagman 
2 CONT
2 CONT =[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDISH%20NOBILITY.htm#EskilMagnusdied1227 '''Project MedLands, Sweden Nobility''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MAGNUS Minnesköld''' (-killed in battle near Lena 31 Jan 1208).  At Bjälbo.  “…B. dux…M. frater ducis B et filius eius Eskillus…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “Kanutus…Sweorum rex” donated property to the 
2 CONC monks of Juleta kloster[31].  “Byrgo Sweorum et Guttorum dux…Philippus frater meus, Magnus et Karolus fratres ducis…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “K…Sweorum rex filius Herjcjs itjdem regis” donated property 
2 CONC to Nydala kloster[32].  m firstly ---.  The name of Magnus´s first wife is not known.  '''married secondly INGRID [Ylva]''' ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus & his first wife had four children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''ESKIL Magnusson''' (-[1227]).  “…B. dux…M. frater ducis B et filius eius Eskillus…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “Kanutus…Sweorum rex” donated property to the monks of Juleta kloster[33].  Lag
2 CONC mand in Västergötland 1219/20.  '''married  (1217) as her second husband, KIRSTIN Nilsdotter, widow of HAAKON "Gallin" Jarl in Norway, daughter of NILS Blaka & his wife Katharina Eriksdotter of Sweden (-1254).'''
2 CONT * b)       '''daughter''' married SIGTRYGG Bengtson [Boberg] (-after 1219). 
2 CONT * c)         '''KARL Magnusson''' (-killed in battle Rotala, Estonia 8 Aug 1220).  Bishop of Linköping.  Chancellor of Sweden. 
2 CONT * d)         '''ELOF Magnusson''' (-bur Alvästra Abbey).  1253/68.  m --- (-bur Alvästra Abbey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus & his second wife had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * e)         '''BENGT Magnusson''' (-4 Jan 1237).  Bishop of Linköping 1220.  m ---.  The name of Bengt´s wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bengt & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* i)          '''MAGNUS Bengtsson''' (-1263).  Lagmand in Östergötland.  m RAGNHILD, daughter of --- (-1262).
2 CONT * f)          '''BIRGER Magnusson''' ([1200]-20/21 Oct 1266, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Icelandic Annals record that "dominus Birgerus Magni filius" was made "comes in Svecia" in 1248[35].  Jarl at Bjälbo.  Regent of Sweden.  Founde
2 CONC r of Stockholm. 
2 CONT
