2 CONT *  '''Bengt Elofsson (winged pi)''' first to have a weapon with an arrow with wings. He is mentioned in Swedish Diplomatariums Huvudkartotek as Omnibus Christi Fidelibus presents Inspecturis, Benedict Eleph son Salutem in Domino S
2 CONC empiternam propane hominumLabilem memoriam, when in a proclamation in February in 1293 Announces that forests and land have been passed on to ' Fröknarna ' Ingeborg and Margaret as the inheritance of their father, the issuer's fat
2 CONC her-in-law, with the consent of the issuer's wife Katarina and her sister Birgitta. Witnesses are Lars Boberg, Rörik Birger'S son and Algot Jonsson, who also together with the issuer are sigillanter.
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Elofsdotter (winged pi);'''married to the knight, the lawyer I Södermanland and the national council Anund Haraldsson (winged Lilja) (DoD 1291) With whom She got her daughter Hclga Anundsdotter (winged lily). Ingebor
2 CONC g inherited according to husband's farm and some land holdings, among other two Gardant I asby outside Arboga.
2 CONT *  '''Cecil Elofsdotter (winged pi),''' married to Magnus Karlsson (Lejonbalk)
2 CONT
2 CONT The name on ELOF wife (R) is unknown. It is if he oeksâ self himself Forde give weapons ("winged pi") that his children did.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDISH%20NOBILITY.htm#BirgerBrosadied1202 Project MedLands SWEDISH NOBILITY]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Magnus Bengtsson Minnesköld (Folkungaätten)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2nd Son of Earl Bengt Folkesson Snivel (Folkunga) and Sigrid Björnsdotter Lakman 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''MAGNUS Minnesköld''' (-killed in battle near Lena 31 Jan 1208).  At Bjälbo.  “…B. dux…M. frater ducis B et filius eius Eskillus…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “Kanutus…Sweorum rex” donated property to th
2 CONC e monks of Juleta kloster[31].  “Byrgo Sweorum et Guttorum dux…Philippus frater meus, Magnus et Karolus fratres ducis…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “K…Sweorum rex filius Herjcjs itjdem regis” donated propert
2 CONC y to Nydala kloster[32].  m firstly ---.  The name of Magnus´s first wife is not known.  m secondly INGRID [Ylva] 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Magnus & his first wife had four children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''ESKIL Magnusson''' (-[1227]).  “…B. dux…M. frater ducis B et filius eius Eskillus…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “Kanutus…Sweorum rex” donated property to the monks of Juleta kloster[33].  Lag
2 CONC mand in Västergötland 1219/20.  m (1217) as her second husband, KIRSTIN Nilsdotter, widow of HAAKON "Gallin" Jarl in Norway, daughter of NILS Blaka & his wife Katharina Eriksdotter of Sweden (-1254).
2 CONT
2 CONT * b)         [34] '''daughter''''  m SIGTRYGG Bengtson [Boberg] (-after 1219). 
2 CONT
2 CONT * c)         '''KARL Magnusson''' (-killed in battle Rotala, Estonia 8 Aug 1220).  Bishop of Linköping.  Chancellor of Sweden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * d)         '''ELOF Magnusson''' (-bur Alvästra Abbey).  1253/68.  m --- (-bur Alvästra Abbey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Magnus & his second wife INGRID [Ylva] had two children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * e)         '''BENGT Magnusson''' (-4 Jan 1237).  Bishop of Linköping 1220.  m ---.  The name of Bengt´s wife is not known.  Bengt & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>i)          '''MAGNUS Bengtsson''' (-1263).  Lagmand in Östergötland.  m RAGNHILD, daughter of (-1262).
2 CONT
2 CONT * f)          '''BIRGER Magnusson''' ([1200]-20/21 Oct 1266, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Icelandic Annals record that "dominus Birgerus Magni filius" was made "comes in Svecia" in 1248[35].  Jarl at Bjälbo.  Regent of Sweden.  Founde
2 CONC r of Stockholm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Project MedLands, Sweden Nobility -
