1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Eirik Bjodaskalle Kåresson==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Eirik Bjodaskalle (in Old Norse : Erik bjödaskali Vikingr-Kåresson , n. 902) was a powerful and influential Viking leader of Oprustader (today Obrestad, Jæren ), in Norway , 10th century. He belonged to a long lineage of warrior
2 CONC s descendants of the legendary Ragnar Lodbrok ; son of lendmann Viking-Kåre .
2 CONT * 902 Eirik was born at Obrestad The parents were Viking Kåre Sigurdsson and Astrid Torleifsdotter
2 CONT * 963 Eirik was alive when his son-in-law Tryggve Olavsson was killed and his daughter Astrid fled home to him.
2 CONT * 52 .... The sons of Eirik Bjodaskalle were Sigurd, Karlshode, Jostein and Torkjell Dyrdil;
2 CONT * 81 .... At the same time, there came also some other great men from Iceland, people who had learned Christianity from Tangbrand; it was Gissur Hvite, son of Teit Kjetilbjørnson, his mother was Ålov, daughter of Bodvar herse, son
2 CONC  of the Viking Corps. Bodvar's brother was Sigurd, father of Eirik Bjodaskalle, father of Astrid, mother of King Olav.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the saga, Eirik Bjodaskalle was a major man on Jæren. He lived on the farm Obrestad in Hå in the 10th century and lived at least in the year 963. Eric's father was Viking-Kåre. He was the grandfather of King Olav Tryg
2 CONC vasson. The name and genealogy of his wife is unknown, but the sagas mention five children of a relationship, all the men had their haciendas in eastern Norway:
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Thorkel Eriksson,''' (n. 928)
2 CONT *''' Dydril Eriksson,''' (n. 931)
2 CONT *''' Erik Eriksson,''' (n. 933)
2 CONT * '''Astrid Eiriksdatter,''' Mother of Olav Trygvasson
2 CONT * '''Sigurd Eiriksson,''' Uncle to Olav Trygvasson and Stormann who served in Holmgard.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==From Snorre Sturlason: Olav Trygveson's story:==
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the saga, Eirik was a big man on Jæren. He lived on the farm Obrestad in Hå in the 10th century and has probably lived approx. 950.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The next thing I want to write about now is about Icelanders."
2 CONT
2 CONT "81. In the same autumn Kjartan Olavson came to Nidaros from Iceland; Kjartan was the son of Olav, the son of Hoskuld, and he was the daughter of Egil Skallagrimson; people say he has been the very best young man ever born in Icel
2 CONC and. There was also Halldor, son of Gudmund at Modruvellir, and Kolbein, son of Tord Frøysgode and brother of Brenne-Flose; the fourth was Sverting, son of Runolf good. All these were Gentiles, and there were many others with them
2 CONC , some mighty and some petty. At the same time, there were some other great men from Iceland, people who had learned Christianity from Tangbrand; it was Gissur Hvite, son of Teit Kjetilbjørnson, his mother was Ålov, daughter of Bo
2 CONC dvar herse, son of the Viking Corps. Bodvar's brother was Sigurd, father of Eirik Bjodaskalle, father of Astrid, mother of King Olav.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==From Snorre Sturlason: Olav the Saint's story:==
2 CONT
2 CONT "69. ... Bjorn and his companion rode their way, and came to Earl of Ragnvald. There they were well received. There were many people who had heard of Bjorn, and all who had seen King Olav knew him both by appearance and voice, for
2 CONC  Bjorn stood up on all things and spoke on the king's behalf. Ingebjorg, the earl's wife, went to Hjalte and kissed him; she knew him, for she was with Olav Trygveson, her brother when Hjalte was there, and Hjalte reckoned friends
2 CONC hip between the king and Vilborg, who was Hjalte's wife: Eirik Bjodaskalle was the father of Astrid, mother of King Olav Trygveson; and Bodvar was the father of Ålov, the mother of Gissur Hvite, the father of Vilborg, and the two,
2 CONC  Eirik and Bodvar, were brothers and sons of Vikinge-Kåre, the countryman at Voss ». 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
2 CONT
