1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * I 1500-tallet var Vadskærgaard ejet af adelsslægten Friis. I sin tidlige ejerhistorie var Vadskærgaard en af Vestjyllands betydningsfulde herregårde.
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT http://adkomstregistrering.navneforskning.ku.dk/gamle/adkomst/a/a000/a193.htm#m03
2 CONT
2 CONT 1522-002 ; Christen Pedersen mester, prior i Dueholm kloster (nævnt 1494-1522) ; Friis (af Vadskærgård) Niels Godskesen "gamle Niels" til Vadskærgård, Skodborg h, (lever 6.5.1549) g m Karen Pallesdatter Juel ; Nykøbing kbst Mors D
2 CONC ueholm kloster ; Nykøbing kbst Mors Helligåndshus, Hellig Trefoldigheds kapel = Sankt Trinitatis kapel, heri de 14 Nødhjælperes alter ; Viborg landsting 1515: u 48 u 83, mon = 83 ? u 83 a, (187); 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1540-120 ; Friis (af Haraldskær) Jørgen Andersen, hr, til Krastrup, biskop i Viborg, (d 1547 før 26.5.) ; Friis (af Vadskærgård) Niels Godskesen "gamle Niels" til Vadskærgård, Skodborg h, (lever 6.5.1549) g m Karen Pallesdatter Ju
2 CONC el ; Mads Mørk bd i (Øster) Ørs, herredsfoged i Skodborg h ; Skodborg herredsting 1520: 112; 1523: 144; 1526: 230; 1528: 238; 1530: 319 329; ; Vejlinggård tidl en hgd, Dybe s, Vandfuld h ; Viborg kbst 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I1430&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vadsk%C3%A6rg%C3%A5rd
2 CONT
2 CONT http://arosleo.dk/doc/hvetbo.pdf, s.8
2 CONT
2 CONT Vadskjærgård (nord for Lemvig) i Skodborg herred.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thyrashm.blogspot.com/2010/08/trring-church-west-jutland-ringkbing_19.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Vadskjærgård belonged in the 1300s to Christiern Nielsen, who sold it to Jep Olsen Lunge. Later it belonged to Niels Friis, who is mentioned 1522, his son Godske Friis 1540-84 and his son Jørgen F. inherited the farm and bought li
2 CONC kewise more estate for it, before he died unmarried 1661. It then went to his brothers' sons Otte Friis of Astrup and Mogens Friis, who later founded Frijsenborg and in 1662 bought Otte's halfpart of V. and some estate. In 1663 he
2 CONC  exchanged the farm to rigsadmiral Ove Gjedde's heirs, of whom the son amtmand Knud Giedde (later of Hastrup, + 1707) became the sole owner. Later owners: Lange, Gjerum Holm, Levetzau, Dahl, Vadum, Gleerup, Andrup, Nyboe, Agger. O
2 CONC utparcelled by Jordlovsudvalget in the 1950s. Main parcel was owned by A. Lindemann and F. Lind Pedersen. The main building was built in 1860 by J.C. Agger.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.danskeherregaarde.dk/manorholder/v/vadskaergaard/ejerhistorie.aspx
