1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ved skiftet efter faderen Anders Jacobsen, overtog Jacob Andersen Vorgaard. Han fik også senere Støvringgaard ved Randers Fjord, men da baade en søn og en datter var barnløse, førtes slægten ikke videre, og godset 
2 CONC gik over til Kaas og Staarupgaard i Fjends herred.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bog: Vor Mand og Råd: Karl Nielsen. Udgiverselskabet vedlandsarkivet for Nørrejylland. 1991.(s. 15)
2 CONT
2 CONT The result was that Axel Jepsen's brother-in-law, ridder and rigsråd Jacob Andersen Bjørn got the farm. He was a great estate-collector. When he married Margrethe Poulsdatter (Fikkesen?), he got as a dowry Tybjerggård, and he was 
2 CONC the owner of Vorgård in Himmerland. And also Støvringgård after his marriage. After his death fru Margrethe managed his estates for many years, but she lived mostly at Støvringgård. From two children her son Anders died unmarried 
2 CONC in 1536. The daughter Dorte was married twice, first time to Christopher Hak of Egholm and second time to Oluf Glob of Vellumgård, but there were no children in either marriage, and the estates went after her death ab.1562 to her 
2 CONC cousin Anne Bjørnsdatter's children. Fru Anne was married to Niels Kaas of Stårupgård and Tårupgård, and two of their sons, Niels and Erik Kaas, inherited Støvringgård.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thyrashm.blogspot.dk/2010/05/stvringgard-east-jutland-randers-amt.html
