0 @N6000000006128010158@ NOTE Though there is no evidence to connect the following Thott family to the one accounted for above, it seems likely that Nils Kyrning, the family pregenitor, was the son of Åge Tordsen (above part 1, no. 2) and his wife Kirsten Kyrn
1 CONC ing. It was notunusual for a son to take the surname of his mother, especially if that family at the time was considered better. As it is, Nils Kyrning, known 1315, knight, died 1354, married 1stly Edle Pedersdatter (Galen) and 2n
1 CONC dly Kirsten N. N. and had issueas follows:
