0 @N6000000000437226980@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> Ii, "The Good" Margrave Of Austria
0 @N6000000002187651511@ NOTE Leopold II, Margrave of Austria
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Leopold II (1050 – October 12, 1095) was a Babenberg Margrave of Austria ruling from 1075 onwards. He was known as Leopold the 'fair'. He was the son of Ernest the Brave and Adelheid, the daughter of Margrave Dedi (or Dedo) II of 
1 CONC Meissen. In the Investiture Dispute, he first sided with Emperor Henry IV, but in 1081 at the Diet of Tulln switched sides under the influence of his wife Itha and Bishop Altmann of Passau. Subsequently, he was deposed by the Empe
1 CONC ror, who gave the fief to Vratislav II of Bohemia, who defeated Leopold in the Battle of Mailberg. Ultimately, Leopold managed to retain his position, but he lost some territory in Southern Moravia. Leopold resided in Gars am Kamp
1 CONC .
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1089 Leopold II helped pay for the construction of Melk Abbey in eastern Austria by donating the land for the new Abbey. A few miles away from Melk Abbey, in eastern Austria, are the ruins of Thunau a Kamp castle, once a summer
1 CONC  residence of Leopold II.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Marriage
1 CONT In 1065 Leopold married Itha (Ida of Cham), countess of Cham (1060-1101), in Cham, Oberphalz, Bavaria. Ida was the daughter of Rapoto IV, Count of Cham, and Mathilde. Ida is said to have died on a crusade.
1 CONT
1 CONT The two had a son, Leopold III, as well as seven daughters who married Dukes and Counts from Carinthia, Bohemia and Germany.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT The Royal Ancestry Bible, Royal Ancestors of 300 Colonial American Families Vol. 3 (chart 2180) by Michel L. Call ISBN 1-933194-22-7 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT  This biography of a member of a European royal house is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Ernest Margrave of Austria
1 CONT 1075-1095 Succeeded by
1 CONT Leopold III 
