0 @N6000000002187570212@ NOTE Judith of Brittany
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Judith of Brittany (982 – 1017) was the daughter of Conan I, Duke of Brittany and the mother of Robert the Magnificent.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the first wife of Richard the Good, Duke of Normandy, whom she married in 996. They had six children:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Richard the Third, succeeded his father in the dukedom;
1 CONT    2. Robert, who succeeded his elder brother;
1 CONT    3. William, called William of Normandy, who became a monk in the Abbey of Fécamp, and died very young in 1025;
1 CONT    4. Alice, married to Renauld, earl of Burgundy;
1 CONT    5. Eleanor, to Baldwin, earl of Flanders;
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT The duchess Judith died in 1017 and was buried in the abbey of Bernay, which she had founded.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Ancestors
1 CONT Judith of Brittany's ancestors in three generations Judith of Brittany Father:
1 CONT Conan I, Duke of Brittany Paternal Grandfather:
1 CONT Judicael Berengar Paternal Great-Grandfather:
1 CONT Berengar II of Neustria
1 CONT Paternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Daughter of Gurvand, Duke of Brittany
1 CONT Paternal Grandmother:
1 CONT Gerberge Paternal Great-Grandfather:
1 CONT Unknown
1 CONT Paternal Great-Grandmother:
1 CONT Unknown
1 CONT Mother:
1 CONT Ermengarde of Anjou Maternal Grandfather:
1 CONT Geoffrey I of Anjou Maternal Great-Grandfather:
1 CONT Fulk II of Anjou
1 CONT Maternal Great-Grandmother:
1 CONT Gerberga of Maine
1 CONT Maternal Grandmother:
1 CONT Adele of Meaux Maternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT Robert of Vermandois
1 CONT Maternal Great-Grandmother:
1 CONT Adelaide of Burgundy
1 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT According to some sources, Judith was born in 956. Source: RoyaList, Leo van de Pas
