0 @N6000000001783499446@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Richard II, called the Good, was the son and heir of Richard the Fearless and Gunnora.  He succeeded his father as Duke of Normandy in 996.   Richard held his own against a peasant insurrection, and helped Robert II of France agai
1 CONC nst the  duchy of Burgundy.  He also repelled an English attack on the Cotentin Peninsula that was led by Ethelred II of England. He pursued a reform of the Norman monasteries.
1 CONT
1 CONT Richard attempted to improve relations with England through his sister's marriage to King Ethelred, but she was strongly disliked by the English. However, this connection later gave his grandson, William the Conqueror, his claim t
1 CONC o the throne of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriages and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT He married firstly (996) Judith of Brittany (982-1017), daughter of Conan I of Brittany,  by whom he had the following issue:
1 CONT Richard III, Duke of Normandy(c.997)
1 CONT Robert, Duke of Normandy (c. 1000)
1 CONT William, monk at Fecamp (d. 1025)
1 CONT Adekaide (Adelaise), married to Renaud I, Count of Burgundy
1 CONT Eleanor, Married to Baldwin IV, Count of Flanders
1 CONT Matilda (d. 1033)
1 CONT
1 CONT Secondly he married Poppa of Envermeu, by whom he had the following issue:
1 CONT Mauger, Archbishop of Rouen
1 CONT William, Count of Arques
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://sbaldw.home.mindspring.com/hproject/prov/richa001.htm>
