1 CONT
1 CONT BALDWIN V also called Baldwin of Lille (d. September I, 1067), countof Flanders who became one of the most influential figures of the 11thcentury Europe. He was an active, enterprising man and greatlyextended his power by wars and
1 CONC  alliances. He obtained from the HolyRoman emperor Henry IV the territory between the Scheldt and theDender as an imperial fief, as well as the margravate of Antwerp. Sopowerful had he become that on the decease of Henry I of Fran
1 CONC ce he wasappointed regent during the minority of Philip I (1060-66). Before hisdeath he saw his eldest daughter Matilda (d. 1083) sharing the Englishthrone with William The Conqueror; saw his eldest son, Baldwin ofMons, in possess
1 CONC ion of Hainault in right of his wife Richilde, heiressof Regnier V ((d. 1036); and saw his second son Robert the Frisian,regent of the county of Holland.
